{"record_type": "item", "metadata": {"thread_id": "019eb3a5-07e3-7163-a098-145f9d55e5f3", "turn_id": "019ef007-e3e7-7783-a060-e504d4091c42", "item_id": "exec-eaf97e2e-a094-48b6-a28c-d45586fd3b02", "rollout_ordinal": 2160, "created_at_ms": 1782144186803, "item_type": "mcpToolCall", "updated_at_ordinal": 2160, "started_at_ms": null, "completed_at_ms": null}, "item": {"type": "mcpToolCall", "id": "exec-eaf97e2e-a094-48b6-a28c-d45586fd3b02", "server": "node_repl", "tool": "js", "status": "completed", "arguments": {"title": "Verificar el título", "code": "var titleState=await tab.playwright.evaluate(()=>Array.from(document.querySelectorAll('input[placeholder=\"Untitled Diagram\"]')).filter(e=>e.offsetWidth||e.offsetHeight||e.getClientRects().length).map(e=>e.value)); nodeRepl.write(JSON.stringify(titleState));"}, "appContext": null, "mcpAppUi": null, "pluginId": null, "readOnlyHint": null, "result": {"content": [{"type": "text", "text": "[\"Modelo de datos - Tesis Karaoke\"]"}], "structuredContent": null, "_meta": {"browser_use": {"url": "https://dbdiagram.io/d"}, "codex/toolSurface": {"backend": "iab", "kind": "browserUse"}}}, "error": null, "durationMs": 69}}
{"record_type": "item", "metadata": {"thread_id": "019eb3a5-07e3-7163-a098-145f9d55e5f3", "turn_id": "019ef007-e3e7-7783-a060-e504d4091c42", "item_id": "item-258", "rollout_ordinal": 2164, "created_at_ms": 1782144227683, "item_type": "agentMessage", "updated_at_ordinal": 2164, "started_at_ms": null, "completed_at_ms": null}, "item": {"type": "agentMessage", "id": "item-258", "text": "Sí. Dejé abierto en `dbdiagram.io` el esquema **“Modelo de datos - Tesis Karaoke”**, con 11 tablas, relaciones y grupos organizados.\n\nEstá como diagrama invitado; para conservarlo debes exportarlo o iniciar sesión.", "phase": "final_answer", "memoryCitation": null, "delivery": null, "questions": null}}
{"record_type": "item", "metadata": {"thread_id": "019eb3a5-07e3-7163-a098-145f9d55e5f3", "turn_id": "019ef0fa-58e1-73e2-a80e-f1b7427a4302", "item_id": "item-259", "rollout_ordinal": 2171, "created_at_ms": 1782159399251, "item_type": "userMessage", "updated_at_ordinal": 2171, "started_at_ms": null, "completed_at_ms": null}, "item": {"type": "userMessage", "id": "item-259", "clientId": "3e283004-ca37-4911-a7ce-4f55487821cd", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "\n# In app browser:\n- The user has the in-app browser open with 1 tab.\n- Current URL: http://localhost:11434/\n\n## My request for Codex:\nsin querer cerré codex y ahora la conexión se perdió, podrías entregarmelo de nuevo\n", "text_elements": []}]}}
{"record_type": "item", "metadata": {"thread_id": "019eb3a5-07e3-7163-a098-145f9d55e5f3", "turn_id": "019ef0fa-58e1-73e2-a80e-f1b7427a4302", "item_id": "item-260", "rollout_ordinal": 2173, "created_at_ms": 1782159420964, "item_type": "agentMessage", "updated_at_ordinal": 2173, "started_at_ms": null, "completed_at_ms": null}, "item": {"type": "agentMessage", "id": "item-260", "text": "Voy a reconstruirlo en una nueva pestaña de `dbdiagram.io` y además guardaré el DBML dentro del proyecto para que no vuelva a perderse aunque cierres Codex o el navegador.", "phase": "commentary", "memoryCitation": null, "delivery": null, "questions": null}}
{"record_type": "item", "metadata": {"thread_id": "019eb3a5-07e3-7163-a098-145f9d55e5f3", "turn_id": "019ef0fa-58e1-73e2-a80e-f1b7427a4302", "item_id": "item-261", "rollout_ordinal": 2187, "created_at_ms": 1782159468440, "item_type": "agentMessage", "updated_at_ordinal": 2187, "started_at_ms": null, "completed_at_ms": null}, "item": {"type": "agentMessage", "id": "item-261", "text": "Primero guardaré una copia permanente del esquema en el proyecto; después la volveré a cargar en una pestaña nueva de `dbdiagram.io`, sin reemplazar la pestaña local que tienes abierta.", "phase": "commentary", "memoryCitation": null, "delivery": null, "questions": null}}
{"record_type": "item", "metadata": {"thread_id": "019eb3a5-07e3-7163-a098-145f9d55e5f3", "turn_id": "019ef0fa-58e1-73e2-a80e-f1b7427a4302", "item_id": "exec-da88f888-beea-4d58-b868-de35ab5324bc", "rollout_ordinal": 2190, "created_at_ms": 1782159502214, "item_type": "fileChange", "updated_at_ordinal": 2190, "started_at_ms": null, "completed_at_ms": null}, "item": {"type": "fileChange", "id": "exec-da88f888-beea-4d58-b868-de35ab5324bc", "changes": [{"path": "C:\\Users\\Diego Tapia\\Desktop\\Pene\\U\\Tesis\\tesis_karaoke\\docs\\modelo_datos_tesis.dbml", "kind": {"type": "add"}, "diff": "// Modelo de datos propuesto para el sistema de análisis vocal\n\nTable cancion {\n  id varchar(80) [pk, note: 'Identificador estable de la canción']\n  titulo varchar(200) [not null]\n  artista varchar(200)\n  original_path varchar(500) [not null]\n  creada_en datetime [not null]\n  activa boolean [not null, default: true]\n}\n\nTable configuracion {\n  id integer [pk, increment]\n  tipo varchar(40) [not null, note: 'referencia, tiempo_real o analisis']\n  version varchar(30) [not null]\n  parametros_json text [not null]\n  hash_config varchar(64) [not null, unique]\n  creada_en datetime [not null]\n}\n\nTable referencia {\n  id varchar(80) [pk]\n  cancion_id varchar(80) [not null]\n  configuracion_id integer [not null]\n  version integer [not null]\n  vocals_path varchar(500) [not null]\n  instrumental_path varchar(500) [not null]\n  pitch_path varchar(500) [not null]\n  modelo_separacion varchar(100) [not null]\n  metodo_pitch varchar(100) [not null]\n  creada_en datetime [not null]\n  estado varchar(30) [not null]\n\n  indexes {\n    (cancion_id, version) [unique]\n  }\n}\n\nTable sesion {\n  id varchar(80) [pk]\n  referencia_id varchar(80) [not null]\n  configuracion_tiempo_real_id integer\n  grabacion_path varchar(500) [not null]\n  fecha_inicio datetime [not null]\n  duracion_segundos decimal(10,3)\n  sample_rate integer [not null]\n  estado varchar(30) [not null]\n}\n\nTable analisis {\n  id varchar(80) [pk]\n  sesion_id varchar(80) [not null]\n  configuracion_id integer [not null]\n  version integer [not null]\n  pitch_usuario_path varchar(500)\n  alineacion_path varchar(500)\n  metodo_alineacion varchar(100) [not null]\n  porcentaje_pitch_valido decimal(6,3)\n  estado varchar(30) [not null]\n  creado_en datetime [not null]\n\n  indexes {\n    (sesion_id, version) [unique]\n  }\n}\n\nTable metrica {\n  analisis_id varchar(80) [pk]\n  error_promedio_cents decimal(10,4)\n  error_firmado_cents decimal(10,4)\n  desviacion_cents decimal(10,4)\n  porcentaje_50 decimal(6,3)\n  porcentaje_100 decimal(6,3)\n  puntos_comparados integer [not null, default: 0]\n  costo_dtw decimal(14,5)\n}\n\nTable segmento {\n  id varchar(80) [pk]\n  analisis_id varchar(80) [not null]\n  inicio_referencia decimal(10,3) [not null]\n  fin_referencia decimal(10,3) [not null]\n  inicio_usuario decimal(10,3) [not null]\n  fin_usuario decimal(10,3) [not null]\n  categoria varchar(50) [not null]\n  magnitud_cents decimal(10,4)\n  duracion_segundos decimal(10,3) [not null]\n  severidad varchar(20) [not null]\n  confianza decimal(5,4) [not null]\n  prioridad integer [not null]\n  evidencia_json text [not null]\n}\n\nTable retroalimentacion {\n  id varchar(80) [pk]\n  analisis_id varchar(80) [not null]\n  tipo_generador varchar(30) [not null, note: 'plantilla, llm_local o llm_remoto']\n  modelo varchar(100)\n  texto text [not null]\n  validada boolean [not null, default: false]\n  creada_en datetime [not null]\n}\n\nTable retroalimentacion_segmento {\n  retroalimentacion_id varchar(80) [not null]\n  segmento_id varchar(80) [not null]\n\n  indexes {\n    (retroalimentacion_id, segmento_id) [pk]\n  }\n}\n\nTable comparacion {\n  id varchar(80) [pk]\n  analisis_anterior_id varchar(80) [not null]\n  analisis_actual_id varchar(80) [not null]\n  comparable boolean [not null]\n  motivo_no_comparable text\n  resumen text\n  creada_en datetime [not null]\n\n  indexes {\n    (analisis_anterior_id, analisis_actual_id) [unique]\n  }\n}\n\nTable cambio {\n  id varchar(80) [pk]\n  comparacion_id varchar(80) [not null]\n  categoria varchar(50) [not null]\n  estado varchar(30) [not null, note: 'mejoro, persistio, empeoro o no_concluyente']\n  variacion decimal(10,4)\n  evidencia_json text [not null]\n}\n\nRef: referencia.cancion_id > cancion.id\nRef: referencia.configuracion_id > configuracion.id\nRef: sesion.referencia_id > referencia.id\nRef: sesion.configuracion_tiempo_real_id > configuracion.id\nRef: analisis.sesion_id > sesion.id\nRef: analisis.configuracion_id > configuracion.id\nRef: metrica.analisis_id - analisis.id\nRef: segmento.analisis_id > analisis.id\nRef: retroalimentacion.analisis_id > analisis.id\nRef: retroalimentacion_segmento.retroalimentacion_id > retroalimentacion.id\nRef: retroalimentacion_segmento.segmento_id > segmento.id\nRef: comparacion.analisis_anterior_id > analisis.id\nRef: comparacion.analisis_actual_id > analisis.id\nRef: cambio.comparacion_id > comparacion.id\n\nTableGroup Preparacion {\n  cancion\n  referencia\n  configuracion\n}\n\nTableGroup Sesiones_y_analisis {\n  sesion\n  analisis\n  metrica\n  segmento\n}\n\nTableGroup Retroalimentacion_y_evolucion {\n  retroalimentacion\n  retroalimentacion_segmento\n  comparacion\n  cambio\n}\n"}], "status": "completed"}}
{"record_type": "item", "metadata": {"thread_id": "019eb3a5-07e3-7163-a098-145f9d55e5f3", "turn_id": "019ef0fa-58e1-73e2-a80e-f1b7427a4302", "item_id": "exec-2d30eacc-9e80-46ee-bed2-6b419f5a6631", "rollout_ordinal": 2199, "created_at_ms": 1782159530782, "item_type": "mcpToolCall", "updated_at_ordinal": 2199, "started_at_ms": null, "completed_at_ms": null}, "item": {"type": "mcpToolCall", "id": "exec-2d30eacc-9e80-46ee-bed2-6b419f5a6631", "server": "node_repl", "tool": "js", "status": "completed", "arguments": {"title": "Reconectar con el navegador", "code": "var { setupBrowserRuntime } = await import(\"C:/Users/Diego Tapia/.codex/plugins/cache/openai-bundled/browser/26.616.51431/scripts/browser-client.mjs\"); await setupBrowserRuntime({ globals: globalThis }); globalThis.browser = await agent.browsers.get(\"iab\"); nodeRepl.write(await browser.documentation());"}, "appContext": null, "mcpAppUi": null, "pluginId": null, "readOnlyHint": null, "result": {"content": [{"type": "text", "text": "## Additional Capabilities\n### Browser Capabilities\n- `visibility`: Use to show or hide the browser to the user, and to determine the browser's current visibility. Keep browser work in the background unless the user asks to see it or live viewing is useful. When the browser should be visible, call set(true).\n  Read with `await (await browser.capabilities.get(\"visibility\")).documentation()`.\n- `viewport`: Controls an explicit browser viewport override for responsive or device-size testing. Use it when a task calls for specific dimensions or breakpoint validation; otherwise leave it unset so the browser uses its normal 1280x720 viewport. Reset temporary overrides before finishing unless the user asked to keep them.\n  Read with `await (await browser.capabilities.get(\"viewport\")).documentation()`.\n### Tab Capabilities\n- `pageAssets`: List assets already observed in the current page state and bundle selected assets into a temporary local artifact.\n  Read with `await (await tab.capabilities.get(\"pageAssets\")).documentation()`.\n\n## Playwright\r\n\r\nPlaywright is a critical part of the JavaScript API available to you.\r\n\r\nYou only have access to a limited subset of the Playwright API, so only call functions that are explicitly defined.\r\nYou do have access to `tab.playwright.evaluate(...)`, but only in a read-only page scope.\r\nUse locators for scoped interactions and targeted checks. For bulk DOM inspection, prefer one bounded read-only `evaluate(...)` that queries and projects the needed data. Avoid loops of locator property calls. In `evaluate(...)`, use basic DOM reads, limit returned elements, and do not assume globals or helpers such as `performance`, `NodeFilter`, `document.createTreeWalker`, or `FormData` exist.\r\n\r\nWhen using Playwright, keep and reuse a recent `tab.playwright.domSnapshot()` when it is available and you need it for locator construction or retry decisions. Treat the latest relevant snapshot as the source of truth for locator construction and retry decisions.\r\n\r\n### Snapshot Discipline\r\n\r\n- Keep and reuse the latest relevant `domSnapshot()` until it proves stale or you need locator ground truth for UI that was not present in it.\r\n- Take a fresh `domSnapshot()` after navigation when you need to orient yourself or construct locators on the new page.\r\n- If a click times out, strict mode fails, or a selector parse error occurs, take a fresh `domSnapshot()` before forming the next locator.\r\n- Construct locators only from what appears in the latest snapshot. Do not guess labels, accessible names, or selectors.\r\n- Do not print full snapshot text repeatedly when a smaller excerpt, a `count()`, a specific attribute, or a direct locator check would answer the question with fewer tokens.\r\n- Do not discover page content by iterating through many results, cards, links, or rows and reading their text or attributes one by one.\r\n- Do not loop over a broad locator with `all()` and call `getAttribute(...)`, `textContent()`, or `innerText()` on each match. Each read crosses the browser boundary and becomes extremely expensive on large pages.\r\n- `locator.getAttribute(...)` is a single-element read, not a batch read. If the locator matches multiple elements, expect a strict-mode error rather than an array of attributes.\r\n- Use one broad observation to orient yourself: usually one fresh snapshot, or one screenshot if the visual structure is clearer than the DOM.\r\n- After that orientation step, narrow to the relevant section or a small number of strong candidates.\r\n- If the page is not getting narrower, do not scale up extraction across more elements. Change strategy instead.\r\n- Do not use `locator(...).allTextContents()`, `locator(\"body\").textContent()`, or `locator(\"body\").innerText()` as exploratory search tools across a page or large container.\r\n- Use broad text or attribute extraction only after you have already identified the exact container or element you need, and only when a smaller scoped check would not answer the question.\r\n- When you need many links, media URLs, or result titles, prefer a single `domSnapshot()` and parse the relevant lines, use the site's own search/filter UI, or navigate directly to a focused results page. Only fall back to per-element reads for a small, already-scoped set of candidates.\r\n- Do not use large body-text dumps, embedded app-state JSON such as `__NEXT_DATA__`, or repeated full-page extraction across multiple candidate pages as an exploratory search strategy.\r\n- Use large text or embedded JSON extraction only after you have already identified the relevant page, or when a site-specific skill explicitly depends on it.\r\n\r\n### Hard Constraints For Playwright In This Runtime\r\n\r\n- Do not pass a regex as `name` to `getByRole(...)` in this environment. Use a plain string `name` only.\r\n- Do not use `.first()`, `.last()`, or `.nth()` unless you have just called `count()` on the same locator and explicitly confirmed why that position is correct.\r\n- Do not click, fill, or press on a locator until you have verified it resolves to exactly one element when uniqueness is not obvious.\r\n- Do not retry the same failing locator without a fresh `domSnapshot()`.\r\n- Do not use a guessed locator as an exploratory probe. If the latest snapshot does not clearly support the locator, do not spend timeout budget testing it.\r\n- Do not assume browser-side Playwright supports the full upstream API surface. If a method is not explicitly known to exist, do not call it.\r\n- Do not assume `locator(...).selectOption(...)` exists in this environment.\r\n\r\n### Required Interaction Recipe\r\n\r\nBefore every click, fill, select-like action, or press:\r\n\r\n1. Reuse the latest relevant `domSnapshot()` when it still contains the locator ground truth you need. Take a fresh one only when it does not.\r\n2. Build the most stable locator from the latest snapshot.\r\n3. If uniqueness is not obvious from the selector itself, call `count()` on that locator.\r\n4. Proceed only if the locator resolves to exactly one element.\r\n5. Perform the action.\r\n6. After the action, collect another observation only when the next decision requires it. Prefer a targeted state check when it answers the question; take a fresh snapshot when you need new locator ground truth.\r\n\r\nIf `count()` is `0`:\r\n\r\n- The selector is wrong, stale, hidden, or the UI state is not ready.\r\n- Do not click anyway.\r\n- Do not wait on that locator to see if it eventually works.\r\n- Re-snapshot and rebuild the locator.\r\n\r\nIf `count()` is greater than `1`:\r\n\r\n- The selector is ambiguous.\r\n- Scope to the correct container or switch to a stronger attribute.\r\n- Do not use `.first()` as a shortcut.\r\n\r\n### Locator Strategy\r\n\r\nBuild locators from what the snapshot actually shows, not what looks visually obvious.\r\n\r\nPrefer the most stable contract, in this order:\r\n\r\n1. `data-testid`\r\n2. Stable `data-*` attributes\r\n3. Stable `href` (prefer exact or strong matches over broad substrings)\r\n4. Scoped semantic role + accessible name using a string `name`\r\n5. Scoped `getByText(...)`\r\n6. Scoped CSS selectors via `locator(...)`\r\n7. A scoped DOM-based click path or node-ID-based click when Playwright cannot produce a unique stable locator\r\n\r\nUse the most specific locator that is still durable.\r\n\r\nTreat a stable `href` as a strong hint, not proof of uniqueness. If multiple elements share the same `href`, scope to the correct card or container and confirm `count()` before clicking.\r\n\r\nTreat generic labels like `Menu`, `Main Menu`, `Help`, `Close`, `Default`, `Color`, `Size`, single-letter size labels such as `S`, `M`, `L`, `XL`, `Sort by`, `Search`, and `Add to cart` as ambiguous by default. Scope them to the correct container before acting.\r\n\r\nOn search results, product grids, carousels, and modal-heavy pages, repeated `href`s and repeated generic labels are ambiguous by default. First identify the stable card or container, then scope the locator inside that container before clicking.\r\n\r\n### Using `getByRole(..., { name })`\r\n\r\n- `name` is the accessible name, which may differ from visible text.\r\n- In the snapshot:\r\n  - `link \"X\"` usually reflects the accessible name.\r\n  - Nested text may be visible text only.\r\n- Use `getByRole` only when the accessible name is clearly present and likely unique in the latest snapshot.\r\n\r\n### Interaction Best Practices\r\n\r\n- Scope before acting: find the right container or section first, then target the child element.\r\n- If you call `count()` on a locator, store the result in a local variable and reuse it unless the DOM changes.\r\n- Match the locator to the actual element type shown in the snapshot (link vs button vs menuitem vs generic text).\r\n- Do not assume every click navigates. If opening a menu or filter, wait for the expected UI state, not page load.\r\n- Prefer structured local signals such as selected control state, visible confirmation text, modal contents, a specific line item, or URL parameters over scraping broad result sections or dumping large parts of the page.\r\n- Do not add explicit `timeoutMs` to routine `click`, `fill`, `check`, or `setChecked` calls unless you have a concrete reason the target is slow to become actionable.\r\n- Reserve explicit timeout values for navigation, state transitions, or other known slow operations.\r\n- If you already know the exact destination URL and no click-side effect matters, prefer `tab.goto(url)` over a brittle locator click.\r\n- Do not reacquire `tab` inside each `node_repl` call. Reuse the existing `tab` binding to save tokens and preserve state. Only reacquire or reassign it when you intentionally switch tabs, after a kernel reset, or after a failed call that did not create the binding.\r\n- Do not use fixed sleeps as a default waiting strategy. After an action, prefer a concrete state check or targeted wait. Take a fresh snapshot when you need new locator ground truth.\r\n- If a fixed delay is truly unavoidable for a known transition, keep it short and follow it immediately with a specific verification step.\r\n\r\n### Error Recovery\r\n\r\n- A strict mode violation means your locator is ambiguous.\r\n- Do not retry the same locator after a strict mode violation.\r\n- After strict mode fails, immediately inspect a fresh snapshot and rebuild the locator using tighter scope, a disambiguating container, or a stable attribute.\r\n- If a checkbox or radio exists but `check()` or `setChecked()` reports that it is hidden or did not change state, stop retrying the underlying input. Click its scoped visible associated `label[for]` or enclosing visible control once, then verify checked state.\r\n- A selector parse error means the locator syntax is invalid in this runtime.\r\n- Do not reuse the same locator form after a selector parse error.\r\n- A timeout usually means the target is missing, hidden, stale, offscreen, not yet rendered, or the selector is too broad.\r\n- Do not retry the same locator immediately after a timeout.\r\n- After a timeout, take a fresh snapshot, confirm the target still exists, and then either refine the locator or fall back to a more stable attribute.\r\n- If role or accessible-name targeting is unstable, fall back deliberately to a stable attribute (`data-*`, `href`, etc.), not brittle CSS structure.\r\n- If two locator attempts fail on the same target, stop escalating complexity on role or text locators. Switch to the most stable visible attribute from the snapshot or use a scoped DOM-based click path.\r\n\r\n### Fallback Guidance\r\n\r\n- Prefer stable `href` values copied from the snapshot over guessed URL patterns.\r\n- Prefer scoped attribute selectors over global text selectors.\r\n- Use `getByText(...)` only when role-based or attribute-based locators are not reliable, and scope it to a container whenever possible.\r\n- Prefer attributes copied directly from the latest snapshot over inferred semantics, fragile CSS chains, or positional selectors.\r\n- Do not invent likely selectors. If the snapshot does not clearly expose a unique target, fetch a fresh snapshot and reassess before acting.\n\n\n## API Reference\nUse this as the supported `agent.browsers.*` surface.\n\n```ts\n// Installed by setupBrowserRuntime({ globals: globalThis }).\nconst browser = await agent.browsers.get(\"iab\");\ninterface Agent {\n  browsers: Browsers; // API for finding and selecting browsers.\n  documentation: Documentation; // API for reading packaged browser-use documentation by name.\n}\n\ninterface Browsers {\n  get(id: string): Promise<Browser>; // Get a browser by id or client type.\n  list(): Promise<Array<{ capabilities: { browser?: Array<{ description: string; id: string }>; tab?: Array<{ description: string; id: string }> }; id: string; metadata?: Record<string, string>; name: string; type: \"iab\" | \"extension\" | \"cdp\" }>>; // List available browsers.\n}\n\ninterface Browser {\n  browserId: string; // Browser id selected by `agent.browsers.get()`.\n  capabilities: BrowserCapabilityCollection; // Browser-scoped optional capabilities advertised by the connected backend; discover IDs with `await browser.capabilities.list()`, then call `await (await browser.capabilities.get(id)).documentation()` for method details.\n  tabs: Tabs; // API for interacting with browser tabs.\n  user: BrowserUser; // Readonly context about tabs in the user's browser windows.\n  documentation(): Promise<string>; // Read browser guidance and the core API reference.\n  nameSession(name: string): Promise<void>; // Name the current browser automation session.\n}\n\ninterface BrowserUser {\n  claimTab(tab: string | BrowserUserTabInfo): Promise<Tab>; // Claim a user tab returned by `openTabs()` and return it as a controllable agent tab.\n\n  openTabs(): Promise<Array<BrowserUserTabInfo>>; // List open top-level tabs across the user's browser windows ordered by `lastOpened` descending.\n}\n\ninterface Tabs {\n\n  finalize(options: FinalizeTabsOptions): Promise<void>; // Finalize the browser session's tabs by cleaning up tabs that are no longer needed.\n  get(id: string): Promise<Tab>; // Get a tab by id.\n  list(): Promise<Array<TabInfo>>; // List open tabs in the browser.\n  new(): Promise<Tab>; // Create and return a new tab in the browser.\n  selected(): Promise<undefined | Tab>; // Return the currently selected tab, if any.\n}\n\ninterface Tab {\n  capabilities: TabCapabilityCollection; // Tab-scoped optional capabilities advertised by the connected backend; discover IDs with `await tab.capabilities.list()`, then call `await (await tab.capabilities.get(id)).documentation()` for method details.\n  clipboard: TabClipboardAPI; // API for interacting with the browser session's clipboard.\n\n  cua: CUAAPI; // API for interacting with the tab via the cua api\n  dev: TabDevAPI; // API for developer-oriented tab inspection.\n  dom_cua: DomCUAAPI; // API for interacting with the tab via the dom based cua api\n  id: string; // A tab's unique identifier\n  playwright: PlaywrightAPI; // API for interacting with the tab via the playwright api\n  back(): Promise<void>; // Navigate this tab back in history.\n  close(): Promise<void>; // Close this tab.\n  forward(): Promise<void>; // Navigate this tab forward in history.\n  getJsDialog(): Promise<undefined | Dialog>; // Get the active JavaScript dialog for this tab, if one is currently open.\n  goto(url: string): Promise<void>; // Open a URL in this tab.\n  reload(): Promise<void>; // Reload this tab.\n  screenshot(options: ScreenshotOptions): Promise<Uint8Array>; // Capture a screenshot of this tab.\n  title(): Promise<undefined | string>; // Get the current title for this tab.\n  url(): Promise<undefined | string>; // Get the current URL for this tab.\n}\n\ninterface CUAAPI {\n  click(options: ClickOptions): Promise<void>; // Click at a coordinate in the current viewport.\n  double_click(options: DoubleClickOptions): Promise<void>; // Double click at a coordinate in the current viewport.\n  \n  drag(options: DragOptions): Promise<void>; // Drag from a point to a point by the provided path.\n  keypress(options: KeypressOptions): Promise<void>; // Press control characters at the current focused element (focus it first via click/dblclick).\n  move(options: MoveOptions): Promise<void>; // Move the mouse to a point by the provided x and y coordinates.\n  scroll(options: ScrollOptions): Promise<void>; // Scroll by a delta from a specific viewport coordinate.\n  type(options: TypeOptions): Promise<void>; // Type text at the current focus.\n}\n\ninterface DomCUAAPI {\n  click(options: DomClickOptions): Promise<void>; // Click a DOM node by its id from the visible DOM snapshot.\n  double_click(options: DomClickOptions): Promise<void>; // Double-click a DOM node by its id.\n  \n  get_visible_dom(): Promise<unknown>; // Return a filtered DOM with node ids for interactable elements.\n  keypress(options: DomKeypressOptions): Promise<void>; // Press control characters at the currently focused element (focus it first via click/dblclick).\n  scroll(options: DomScrollOptions): Promise<void>; // Scroll either the page or a specific node (if node_id provided) by deltas.\n  type(options: DomTypeOptions): Promise<void>; // Type text into the currently focused element (focus via click first).\n}\n\ninterface PlaywrightAPI {\n  domSnapshot(): Promise<string>; // Return a snapshot of the current DOM as a string, including expanded iframe body content when available.\n\n  evaluate<TResult, TArg>(pageFunction: PlaywrightEvaluateFunction<TArg, TResult>, arg?: TArg, options?: PlaywrightEvaluateOptions): Promise<TResult>; // Evaluate JavaScript in a read-only page scope.\n  expectNavigation<T>(action: () => Promise<T>, options: { timeoutMs?: number; url?: string; waitUntil?: LoadState }): Promise<T>; // Expect a navigation triggered by an action.\n  frameLocator(frameSelector: string): PlaywrightFrameLocator; // Create a frame-scoped locator builder.\n  getByLabel(text: TextMatcher, options: { exact?: boolean }): PlaywrightLocator; // Find elements by label text within the page.\n  getByPlaceholder(text: TextMatcher, options: { exact?: boolean }): PlaywrightLocator; // Find elements by placeholder text within the page.\n  getByRole(role: string, options: { exact?: boolean; name?: TextMatcher }): PlaywrightLocator; // Find elements by ARIA role within the page.\n  getByTestId(testId: string): PlaywrightLocator; // Find elements by test id within the page.\n  getByText(text: TextMatcher, options: { exact?: boolean }): PlaywrightLocator; // Find elements by text within the page.\n  locator(selector: string): PlaywrightLocator; // Create a locator scoped to this tab.\n  waitForEvent(event: \"download\", options?: WaitForEventOptions): Promise<PlaywrightDownload>; // Wait for the next event on the page.\n\n  waitForLoadState(options: PageWaitForLoadStateOptions): Promise<void>; // Wait for the page to reach a specific load state.\n  waitForTimeout(timeoutMs: number): Promise<void>; // Wait for a fixed duration.\n  waitForURL(url: string, options: PageWaitForURLOptions): Promise<void>; // Wait for the page URL to match the provided value.\n}\n\ninterface PlaywrightFrameLocator {\n  frameLocator(frameSelector: string): PlaywrightFrameLocator; // Create a locator scoped to a nested frame.\n  getByLabel(text: TextMatcher, options: { exact?: boolean }): PlaywrightLocator; // Find elements by label within this frame.\n  getByPlaceholder(text: TextMatcher, options: { exact?: boolean }): PlaywrightLocator; // Find elements by placeholder within this frame.\n  getByRole(role: string, options: { exact?: boolean; name?: TextMatcher }): PlaywrightLocator; // Find elements by ARIA role within this frame.\n  getByTestId(testId: string): PlaywrightLocator; // Find elements by test id within this frame.\n  getByText(text: TextMatcher, options: { exact?: boolean }): PlaywrightLocator; // Find elements by text within this frame.\n  locator(selector: string): PlaywrightLocator; // Create a locator scoped to this frame.\n}\n\ninterface PlaywrightLocator {\n  all(): Promise<Array<PlaywrightLocator>>; // Resolve to a list of locators for each matched element.\n  allTextContents(options: { timeoutMs?: number }): Promise<Array<string>>; // Return `textContent` for *all* elements matched by this locator.\n  and(locator: PlaywrightLocator): PlaywrightLocator; // Return a locator matching elements that satisfy both this locator and `locator`.\n  check(options: LocatorCheckOptions): Promise<void>; // Check a checkbox or switch-like control.\n  click(options: LocatorClickOptions): Promise<void>; // Click the element matched by this locator.\n  count(): Promise<number>; // Number of elements matching this locator.\n  dblclick(options: LocatorClickOptions): Promise<void>; // Double-click the element matched by this locator.\n  downloadMedia(options: LocatorDownloadMediaOptions): Promise<void>; // Trigger a media download for the first matched element.\n  fill(value: string, options: { timeoutMs?: number }): Promise<void>; // Replace the element's value with the provided text.\n  filter(options: LocatorFilterOptions): PlaywrightLocator; // Narrow this locator by additional constraints.\n  first(): PlaywrightLocator; // Return a locator pointing at the first matched element.\n  getAttribute(name: string, options: { timeoutMs?: number }): Promise<null | string>; // Return an attribute value from the first matched element.\n  getByLabel(text: TextMatcher, options: { exact?: boolean }): PlaywrightLocator; // Find elements by label text, scoped to this locator.\n  getByPlaceholder(text: TextMatcher, options: { exact?: boolean }): PlaywrightLocator; // Find elements by placeholder text, scoped to this locator.\n  getByRole(role: string, options: { exact?: boolean; name?: TextMatcher }): PlaywrightLocator; // Find elements by ARIA role, scoped to this locator.\n  getByTestId(testId: string): PlaywrightLocator; // Find elements by test id, scoped to this locator.\n  getByText(text: TextMatcher, options: { exact?: boolean }): PlaywrightLocator; // Find elements by text content, scoped to this locator.\n  innerText(options: { timeoutMs?: number }): Promise<string>; // Return the rendered (visible) text of the first matched element.\n  isEnabled(): Promise<boolean>; // Whether the first matched element is currently enabled.\n  isVisible(): Promise<boolean>; // Whether the first matched element is currently visible.\n  last(): PlaywrightLocator; // Return a locator pointing at the last matched element.\n  locator(selector: string, options: LocatorLocatorOptions): PlaywrightLocator; // Create a descendant locator scoped to this locator.\n  nth(index: number): PlaywrightLocator; // Return a locator pointing at the Nth matched element.\n  or(locator: PlaywrightLocator): PlaywrightLocator; // Return a locator matching elements that satisfy either this locator or `locator`.\n  press(value: string, options: { timeoutMs?: number }): Promise<void>; // Press a keyboard key while this locator is focused.\n  selectOption(value: SelectOptionInput | Array<SelectOptionInput>, options: { timeoutMs?: number }): Promise<void>; // Select one or more options on a native `<select>` element.\n  setChecked(checked: boolean, options: LocatorCheckOptions): Promise<void>; // Set a checkbox or switch-like control to a checked/unchecked state.\n  textContent(options: { timeoutMs?: number }): Promise<null | string>; // Return the raw textContent of the first matched element (or null if missing).\n  type(value: string, options: { timeoutMs?: number }): Promise<void>; // Type text into the element without clearing existing content.\n  uncheck(options: LocatorCheckOptions): Promise<void>; // Uncheck a checkbox or switch-like control.\n  waitFor(options: LocatorWaitForOptions): Promise<void>; // Wait for the element to reach a specific state.\n}\n\ninterface PlaywrightDownload {\n\n}\n\ninterface TabClipboardAPI {\n  read(): Promise<Array<TabClipboardItem>>; // Read clipboard items, including text and binary payloads.\n  readText(): Promise<string>; // Read plain text from the browser clipboard.\n  write(items: Array<TabClipboardItem>): Promise<void>; // Write clipboard items.\n  writeText(text: string): Promise<void>; // Write plain text to the browser clipboard.\n}\n\ninterface TabDevAPI {\n  logs(options: TabDevLogsOptions): Promise<Array<TabDevLogEntry>>; // Read console log messages captured for this tab.\n}\n\ninterface AlertDialog {\n  type: \"alert\";\n  dismiss(): Promise<void>;\n}\n\ninterface BeforeUnloadDialog {\n  type: \"beforeunload\";\n  dismiss(): Promise<void>;\n}\n\ninterface ConfirmDialog {\n  type: \"confirm\";\n  accept(): Promise<void>;\n  dismiss(): Promise<void>;\n}\n\ninterface Documentation {\n  get(name: string): Promise<string>; // Read packaged documentation by its extensionless relative path.\n}\n\ninterface PromptDialog {\n  type: \"prompt\";\n  accept(text: string): Promise<void>;\n  dismiss(): Promise<void>;\n}\n\ntype BrowserCapabilityCollection = {\n  get(id: string): Promise<unknown>;\n  list(): Promise<Array<{ id: string; description: string }>>;\n};\n\ninterface BrowserUserTabInfo {\n  id: string; // Opaque identifier for this browser tab.\n  lastOpened?: string; // ISO 8601 timestamp for the last time the tab was opened or focused.\n  tabGroup?: string; // User-visible tab group name when the tab belongs to one.\n  title?: string; // User-visible tab title.\n  url?: string; // Current tab URL.\n}\n\ninterface TabsContentOptions {\n\n  timeoutMs?: number; // Maximum time to wait for each page load, in milliseconds.\n  urls: Array<string>; // URLs to load in temporary background tabs.\n}\n\ninterface TabsContentResult {\n\n  title: null | string; // The resolved page title when available.\n  url: string; // The resolved page URL when available, otherwise the requested URL.\n}\n\ninterface FinalizeTabsOptions {\n  keep?: Array<FinalizeTabsKeep>; // Explicit tab dispositions to preserve after cleanup.\n}\n\ninterface TabInfo {\n  id: string; // Metadata describing an open tab.\n  title?: string;\n  url?: string;\n}\n\ntype TabCapabilityCollection = {\n  get(id: string): Promise<unknown>;\n  list(): Promise<Array<{ id: string; description: string }>>;\n};\n\ntype Dialog = AlertDialog | BeforeUnloadDialog | ConfirmDialog | PromptDialog;\n\ntype ScreenshotOptions = {\n  clip?: ClipRect; // Crop to a specific rectangle instead of the full viewport.\n  fullPage?: boolean; // Capture the full page instead of the viewport.\n};\n\ntype ClickOptions = {\n  button?: number; // Mouse button (1-left, 2-middle/wheel, 3-right, 4-back, 5-forward).\n  keypress?: Array<string>; // Modifier keys held during the click.\n  x: number;\n  y: number;\n};\n\ntype DoubleClickOptions = {\n  keypress?: Array<string>; // Modifier keys held during the double click.\n  x: number;\n  y: number;\n};\n\ntype DragOptions = {\n  keys?: Array<string>; // Optional modifier keys held during the drag.\n  path: Array<{ x: number; y: number }>; // Drag path as a list of points.\n};\n\ntype KeypressOptions = {\n  keys: Array<string>; // Key combination to press.\n};\n\ntype MoveOptions = {\n  keys?: Array<string>; // Optional modifier keys held while moving.\n  x: number;\n  y: number;\n};\n\ntype ScrollOptions = {\n  keypress?: Array<string>; // Modifier keys held during scroll.\n  scrollX: number;\n  scrollY: number;\n  x: number;\n  y: number;\n};\n\ntype TypeOptions = {\n  text: string;\n};\n\ntype DomClickOptions = {\n  node_id: string; // Node id from `get_visible_dom()`.\n};\n\ntype DomKeypressOptions = {\n  keys: Array<string>; // Key combination to press.\n};\n\ntype DomScrollOptions = {\n  node_id?: string; // Optional node id to scroll within.\n  x: number; // Horizontal scroll delta.\n  y: number; // Vertical scroll delta.\n};\n\ntype DomTypeOptions = {\n  text: string; // Text to type into the currently focused element.\n};\n\ntype ElementInfoOptions = {\n  includeNonInteractable?: boolean; // When true, include non-interactable elements in addition to interactable targets.\n  x: number;\n  y: number;\n};\n\ntype ElementInfo = {\n  ariaName?: string | null; // Accessible name if available.\n  boundingBox?: ElementInfoRect | null; // Element bounds in screenshot coordinates.\n  nodeId?: number | null; // Backend node id that can be passed to DOM-inspection APIs when available.\n  preview: string; // Compact human-readable node preview.\n  role?: string | null; // Computed ARIA role if available.\n  selector: ElementInfoSelector; // Suggested selector data for this element.\n  tagName: string; // Lowercased HTML tag name.\n  testId?: string | null; // Configured test id attribute if present.\n  visibleText?: string | null; // Rendered visible text, selected option text, or visible form value when available.\n};\n\ntype ElementScreenshotOptions = {\n  includeNonInteractable?: boolean; // When true, highlight non-interactable elements in addition to interactable targets.\n  x: number;\n  y: number;\n};\n\ntype PlaywrightEvaluateFunction<TArg, TResult> = string | (arg: TArg) => TResult | Promise<TResult>;\n\ntype PlaywrightEvaluateOptions = {\n  timeoutMs?: number; // Maximum time to spend setting up the read-only DOM scope and running the script.\n};\n\ntype LoadState = \"load\" | \"domcontentloaded\" | \"networkidle\";\n\ntype TextMatcher = string | RegExp;\n\ntype WaitForEventOptions = {\n  timeoutMs?: number;\n};\n\ntype PageWaitForLoadStateOptions = {\n  state?: LoadState;\n  timeoutMs?: number;\n};\n\ntype PageWaitForURLOptions = {\n  timeoutMs?: number;\n  waitUntil?: WaitUntil;\n};\n\ntype LocatorCheckOptions = {\n  force?: boolean;\n  timeoutMs?: number;\n};\n\ntype LocatorClickOptions = {\n  button?: MouseButton;\n  force?: boolean;\n  modifiers?: Array<KeyboardModifier>;\n  timeoutMs?: number;\n};\n\ntype LocatorDownloadMediaOptions = {\n  timeoutMs?: number;\n};\n\ntype LocatorFilterOptions = {\n  has?: PlaywrightLocator;\n  hasNot?: PlaywrightLocator;\n  hasNotText?: TextMatcher;\n  hasText?: TextMatcher;\n  visible?: boolean;\n};\n\ntype LocatorLocatorOptions = {\n  has?: PlaywrightLocator;\n  hasNot?: PlaywrightLocator;\n  hasNotText?: TextMatcher;\n  hasText?: TextMatcher;\n};\n\ntype SelectOptionInput = string | SelectOptionDescriptor;\n\ntype LocatorWaitForOptions = {\n  state: WaitForState;\n  timeoutMs?: number;\n};\n\ntype TabClipboardItem = {\n  entries: Array<TabClipboardEntry>;\n  presentationStyle?: \"unspecified\" | \"inline\" | \"attachment\";\n};\n\ninterface TabDevLogsOptions {\n  filter?: string; // Optional substring filter applied to the rendered log message.\n  levels?: Array<\"debug\" | \"info\" | \"log\" | \"warn\" | \"error\" | \"warning\">; // Optional levels to include.\n  limit?: number; // Maximum number of logs to return.\n}\n\ninterface TabDevLogEntry {\n  level: \"debug\" | \"info\" | \"log\" | \"warn\" | \"error\"; // Console log level.\n  message: string; // Rendered log message text.\n  timestamp: string; // ISO 8601 timestamp for when the runtime captured the log.\n  url?: string; // Source URL reported by the browser runtime, when available.\n}\n\ntype TabsContentType = \"html\" | \"text\" | \"domSnapshot\";\n\ninterface FinalizeTabsKeep {\n  status: FinalizeTabStatus; // Where the kept tab belongs after cleanup.\n  tab: string | Tab | TabInfo; // Tab object to keep open after browser cleanup.\n}\n\ntype ClipRect = {\n  height: number;\n  width: number;\n  x: number;\n  y: number;\n};\n\ntype ElementInfoRect = {\n  height: number;\n  width: number;\n  x: number;\n  y: number;\n};\n\ntype ElementInfoSelector = {\n  candidates: Array<string>; // Ranked selector candidates for the element.\n  frameSelectors?: Array<string>; // Frame selectors to enter before using the element selector.\n  primary?: string | null; // The preferred selector for the element when available.\n};\n\ntype WaitUntil = LoadState | \"commit\";\n\ntype MouseButton = \"left\" | \"right\" | \"middle\";\n\ntype KeyboardModifier = \"Alt\" | \"Control\" | \"ControlOrMeta\" | \"Meta\" | \"Shift\";\n\ntype SelectOptionDescriptor = {\n  index?: number;\n  label?: string;\n  value?: string;\n};\n\ntype WaitForState = \"attached\" | \"detached\" | \"visible\" | \"hidden\";\n\ntype TabClipboardEntry = {\n  base64?: string;\n  mimeType: string;\n  text?: string;\n};\n\ntype FinalizeTabStatus = \"handoff\" | \"deliverable\";\n```\n"}], "structuredContent": null, "_meta": {"browser_use": {}, "codex/toolSurface": {"backend": "iab", "kind": "browserUse"}}}, "error": null, "durationMs": 1383}}
{"record_type": "item", "metadata": {"thread_id": "019eb3a5-07e3-7163-a098-145f9d55e5f3", "turn_id": "019ef0fa-58e1-73e2-a80e-f1b7427a4302", "item_id": "exec-7e9c0c1b-9251-4eed-b36c-65a989703e1b", "rollout_ordinal": 2204, "created_at_ms": 1782159546934, "item_type": "mcpToolCall", "updated_at_ordinal": 2204, "started_at_ms": null, "completed_at_ms": null}, "item": {"type": "mcpToolCall", "id": "exec-7e9c0c1b-9251-4eed-b36c-65a989703e1b", "server": "node_repl", "tool": "js", "status": "completed", "arguments": {"title": "Abrir nuevamente dbdiagram.io", "code": "await (await browser.capabilities.get(\"visibility\")).set(true); var diagramTab = await browser.tabs.new(); await diagramTab.goto(\"https://dbdiagram.io/d\"); await diagramTab.playwright.waitForLoadState({state:\"domcontentloaded\",timeoutMs:30000}).catch(()=>{}); nodeRepl.write(JSON.stringify({url:await diagramTab.url(),title:await diagramTab.title()}));"}, "appContext": null, "mcpAppUi": null, "pluginId": null, "readOnlyHint": null, "result": {"content": [{"type": "text", "text": "{\"url\":\"https://dbdiagram.io/d\",\"title\":\"dbdiagram.io - Database Relationship Diagrams Design Tool\"}"}], "structuredContent": null, "_meta": {"browser_use": {}, "codex/toolSurface": {"backend": "iab", "kind": "browserUse"}}}, "error": null, "durationMs": 2275}}
{"record_type": "item", "metadata": {"thread_id": "019eb3a5-07e3-7163-a098-145f9d55e5f3", "turn_id": "019ef0fa-58e1-73e2-a80e-f1b7427a4302", "item_id": "exec-70988489-bfac-4825-8345-29d969f31d32", "rollout_ordinal": 2209, "created_at_ms": 1782159559268, "item_type": "mcpToolCall", "updated_at_ordinal": 2209, "started_at_ms": null, "completed_at_ms": null}, "item": {"type": "mcpToolCall", "id": "exec-70988489-bfac-4825-8345-29d969f31d32", "server": "node_repl", "tool": "js", "status": "completed", "arguments": {"title": "Preparar el editor", "code": "nodeRepl.write(await diagramTab.playwright.domSnapshot());"}, "appContext": null, "mcpAppUi": null, "pluginId": null, "readOnlyHint": null, "result": {"content": [{"type": "text", "text": "- banner:\n  - button \"dbdiagram-logo Personal\":\n    - img \"dbdiagram-logo\"\n    - generic: Personal\n  - generic: /\n  - img \"unsaved\"\n  - textbox:\n    - /placeholder: Untitled Diagram\n  - button:\n- code:\n  - generic: \"1\"\n  - generic: \"2\"\n  - generic: \"3\"\n  - generic: \n  - generic: \"4\"\n  - generic: \"5\"\n  - generic: \"6\"\n  - generic: \"7\"\n  - generic: \"8\"\n  - generic: \"9\"\n  - generic: \n  - generic: \"10\"\n  - generic: \"11\"\n  - generic: \"12\"\n  - generic: \"13\"\n  - generic: \"14\"\n  - generic: \"15\"\n  - generic: \"16\"\n  - generic: \n  - generic: \"17\"\n  - generic: \"18\"\n  - generic: \"19\"\n  - generic: \"20\"\n  - generic: \"21\"\n  - generic: \"22\"\n  - generic: \"23\"\n  - generic: \"24\"\n  - generic: \"25\"\n  - generic: \"26\"\n  - generic: \"27\"\n  - generic: // Use DBML to define your database structure\n  - generic: \"// Docs: https://dbml.dbdiagram.io/docs\"\n  - generic: \"Table follows {\"\n  - generic: following_user_id integer\n  - generic: followed_user_id integer\n  - generic: created_at timestamp\n  - generic: \"}\"\n  - generic: \"Table users {\"\n  - generic: id integer [primary key]\n  - generic: username varchar\n  - generic: role varchar\n  - generic: created_at timestamp\n  - generic: \"}\"\n  - generic: \"Table posts {\"\n  - generic: id integer [primary key]\n  - generic: title varchar\n  - generic: \"body text [note: 'Content of the post']\"\n  - generic: user_id integer [not null]\n  - generic: status varchar\n  - generic: created_at timestamp\n  - generic: \"}\"\n  - generic: \"Ref user_posts: posts.user_id > users.id // many-to-one\"\n  - textbox \"Editor content;Press Alt+F1 for Accessibility Options.\": \"// Use DBML to define your database structure // Docs: https://dbml.dbdiagram.io/docs Table follows { following_user_id integer followed_user_id integer created_at timestamp } Table users {\"\n- link \"banner image 🔥 Embed Dashboards In 15 Minutes 🔥 Fast, flexible, and pixel-perfect embedded analytics is just a snippet away.\":\n  - /url: https://www.holistics.io/product/embedded-analytics/?utm_source=dbdiagram&utm_medium=ads\n  - img \"banner image\"\n  - generic: 🔥 Embed Dashboards In 15 Minutes 🔥\n  - paragraph: Fast, flexible, and pixel-perfect embedded analytics is just a snippet away.\n- button:\n- generic: 34%\n- button:\n- button \"1\":\n  - generic: \"1\"\n- button:\n- button:\n- generic: \"2\"\n- button \"3\":\n  - generic: \"3\"\n- button \"4\":\n  - generic: \"4\"\n- button:\n- button:\n- button \"Close\":\n- generic: Your browser does not support the video tag.\n- heading \"🤖 AI Assistant Joins the Party!\" [level=2]\n- paragraph: Chat naturally to create/refine database diagrams, add tables & relationships, or get suggestions on indexes and data types.\n- button \"Learn more\":\n  - generic: Learn more\n- alert\n- alert\n- complementary\n- complementary"}], "structuredContent": null, "_meta": {"browser_use": {"url": "https://dbdiagram.io/d"}, "codex/toolSurface": {"backend": "iab", "kind": "browserUse"}}}, "error": null, "durationMs": 69}}
{"record_type": "item", "metadata": {"thread_id": "019eb3a5-07e3-7163-a098-145f9d55e5f3", "turn_id": "019ef0fa-58e1-73e2-a80e-f1b7427a4302", "item_id": "exec-781735bc-a11e-44d1-ab9e-d3763d2d577f", "rollout_ordinal": 2214, "created_at_ms": 1782159575574, "item_type": "mcpToolCall", "updated_at_ordinal": 2214, "started_at_ms": null, "completed_at_ms": null}, "item": {"type": "mcpToolCall", "id": "exec-781735bc-a11e-44d1-ab9e-d3763d2d577f", "server": "node_repl", "tool": "js", "status": "completed", "arguments": {"title": "Cerrar aviso del editor", "code": "var closeNotice=diagramTab.playwright.getByRole(\"button\",{name:\"Close\",exact:true}); var closeCount=await closeNotice.count(); if(closeCount===1) await closeNotice.click(); nodeRepl.write(JSON.stringify({closeCount}));"}, "appContext": null, "mcpAppUi": null, "pluginId": null, "readOnlyHint": null, "result": {"content": [{"type": "text", "text": "{\"closeCount\":1}"}], "structuredContent": null, "_meta": {"browser_use": {"url": "https://dbdiagram.io/d"}, "codex/toolSurface": {"backend": "iab", "kind": "browserUse"}}}, "error": null, "durationMs": 561}}
{"record_type": "item", "metadata": {"thread_id": "019eb3a5-07e3-7163-a098-145f9d55e5f3", "turn_id": "019ef0fa-58e1-73e2-a80e-f1b7427a4302", "item_id": "exec-3667dc66-273d-4660-9ffc-4738dea09850", "rollout_ordinal": 2219, "created_at_ms": 1782159593174, "item_type": "mcpToolCall", "updated_at_ordinal": 2219, "started_at_ms": null, "completed_at_ms": null}, "item": {"type": "mcpToolCall", "id": "exec-3667dc66-273d-4660-9ffc-4738dea09850", "server": "node_repl", "tool": "js", "status": "completed", "arguments": {"title": "Restaurar el modelo de datos", "code": "var fs = await import(\"node:fs/promises\"); var schemaText = await fs.readFile(\"C:/Users/Diego Tapia/Desktop/Pene/U/Tesis/tesis_karaoke/docs/modelo_datos_tesis.dbml\",\"utf8\"); var schemaEditor=diagramTab.playwright.getByRole(\"textbox\",{name:\"Editor content;Press Alt+F1 for Accessibility Options.\",exact:true}); var schemaCount=await schemaEditor.count(); if(schemaCount!==1) throw new Error(\"Editor ambiguo\"); await schemaEditor.fill(schemaText); var titleVisible=diagramTab.playwright.locator('input[placeholder=\"Untitled Diagram\"]').filter({visible:true}); var titleVisibleCount=await titleVisible.count(); if(titleVisibleCount!==1) throw new Error(\"Título ambiguo\"); await titleVisible.fill(\"Modelo de datos - Tesis Karaoke\"); nodeRepl.write(JSON.stringify({schemaCount,titleVisibleCount,chars:schemaText.length}));"}, "appContext": null, "mcpAppUi": null, "pluginId": null, "readOnlyHint": null, "result": {"content": [{"type": "text", "text": "{\"schemaCount\":1,\"titleVisibleCount\":1,\"chars\":4545}"}], "structuredContent": null, "_meta": {"browser_use": {"url": "https://dbdiagram.io/d"}, "codex/toolSurface": {"backend": "iab", "kind": "browserUse"}}}, "error": null, "durationMs": 268}}
{"record_type": "item", "metadata": {"thread_id": "019eb3a5-07e3-7163-a098-145f9d55e5f3", "turn_id": "019ef0fa-58e1-73e2-a80e-f1b7427a4302", "item_id": "item-262", "rollout_ordinal": 2223, "created_at_ms": 1782159607645, "item_type": "agentMessage", "updated_at_ordinal": 2223, "started_at_ms": null, "completed_at_ms": null}, "item": {"type": "agentMessage", "id": "item-262", "text": "El esquema ya está cargado nuevamente. Estoy comprobando que las tablas y relaciones se hayan renderizado correctamente antes de dejarte la pestaña abierta.", "phase": "commentary", "memoryCitation": null, "delivery": null, "questions": null}}
{"record_type": "item", "metadata": {"thread_id": "019eb3a5-07e3-7163-a098-145f9d55e5f3", "turn_id": "019ef0fa-58e1-73e2-a80e-f1b7427a4302", "item_id": "exec-fe230e39-c8c9-4739-95b8-6dd59cf9cc45", "rollout_ordinal": 2226, "created_at_ms": 1782159613672, "item_type": "mcpToolCall", "updated_at_ordinal": 2226, "started_at_ms": null, "completed_at_ms": null}, "item": {"type": "mcpToolCall", "id": "exec-fe230e39-c8c9-4739-95b8-6dd59cf9cc45", "server": "node_repl", "tool": "js", "status": "completed", "arguments": {"title": "Verificar el diagrama restaurado", "code": "await diagramTab.playwright.waitForTimeout(1200); var titleCheck=await diagramTab.playwright.evaluate(()=>Array.from(document.querySelectorAll('input[placeholder=\"Untitled Diagram\"]')).filter(e=>e.offsetWidth||e.offsetHeight||e.getClientRects().length).map(e=>e.value)); var restoredShot=await diagramTab.screenshot({fullPage:false}); await nodeRepl.emitImage(restoredShot); nodeRepl.write(JSON.stringify({title:titleCheck,url:await diagramTab.url()}));"}, "appContext": null, "mcpAppUi": null, "pluginId": null, "readOnlyHint": null, "result": {"content": [{"type": "text", "text": "{\"title\":[\"Modelo de datos - Tesis Karaoke\"],\"url\":\"https://dbdiagram.io/d\"}"}, {"type": "image", "data": "", "mimeType": "image/jpeg", "_meta": {"codex/imageDetail": "original"}}], "structuredContent": null, "_meta": {"browser_use": {}, "codex/toolSurface": {"backend": "iab", "kind": "browserUse"}}}, "error": null, "durationMs": 1390}}
{"record_type": "item", "metadata": {"thread_id": "019eb3a5-07e3-7163-a098-145f9d55e5f3", "turn_id": "019ef0fa-58e1-73e2-a80e-f1b7427a4302", "item_id": "exec-a65e0c97-80dc-4c47-ad01-d2c66b37c41d", "rollout_ordinal": 2231, "created_at_ms": 1782159625734, "item_type": "mcpToolCall", "updated_at_ordinal": 2231, "started_at_ms": null, "completed_at_ms": null}, "item": {"type": "mcpToolCall", "id": "exec-a65e0c97-80dc-4c47-ad01-d2c66b37c41d", "server": "node_repl", "tool": "js", "status": "completed", "arguments": {"title": "Dejar el diagrama abierto", "code": "await browser.tabs.finalize({keep:[{tab:diagramTab,status:\"deliverable\"}]}); nodeRepl.write(\"finalized\");"}, "appContext": null, "mcpAppUi": null, "pluginId": null, "readOnlyHint": null, "result": {"content": [{"type": "text", "text": "finalized"}], "structuredContent": null, "_meta": {"browser_use": {}, "codex/toolSurface": {"backend": "iab", "kind": "browserUse"}}}, "error": null, "durationMs": 42}}
{"record_type": "item", "metadata": {"thread_id": "019eb3a5-07e3-7163-a098-145f9d55e5f3", "turn_id": "019ef0fa-58e1-73e2-a80e-f1b7427a4302", "item_id": "item-263", "rollout_ordinal": 2235, "created_at_ms": 1782159638327, "item_type": "agentMessage", "updated_at_ordinal": 2235, "started_at_ms": null, "completed_at_ms": null}, "item": {"type": "agentMessage", "id": "item-263", "text": "Restauré el diagrama en una nueva pestaña de `dbdiagram.io` y mantuve tu pestaña local.\n\nTambién guardé una copia permanente:\n\n[modelo_datos_tesis.dbml](<C:\\Users\\Diego Tapia\\Desktop\\Pene\\U\\Tesis\\tesis_karaoke\\docs\\modelo_datos_tesis.dbml>)", "phase": "final_answer", "memoryCitation": null, "delivery": null, "questions": null}}
{"record_type": "item", "metadata": {"thread_id": "019eb3a5-07e3-7163-a098-145f9d55e5f3", "turn_id": "019ef101-b04f-7f32-a359-1411515b670d", "item_id": "item-264", "rollout_ordinal": 2242, "created_at_ms": 1782159880363, "item_type": "userMessage", "updated_at_ordinal": 2242, "started_at_ms": null, "completed_at_ms": null}, "item": {"type": "userMessage", "id": "item-264", "clientId": "32de55e6-272f-4fb5-a37d-1d36d0f0fe2e", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "\n# In app browser:\n- The user has the in-app browser open with 3 tabs.\n- Current URL: https://dbdiagram.io\n\n## My request for Codex:\nal iniciar sesión se perdió el link\n", "text_elements": []}]}}
{"record_type": "item", "metadata": {"thread_id": "019eb3a5-07e3-7163-a098-145f9d55e5f3", "turn_id": "019ef101-b04f-7f32-a359-1411515b670d", "item_id": "item-265", "rollout_ordinal": 2244, "created_at_ms": 1782159892754, "item_type": "agentMessage", "updated_at_ordinal": 2244, "started_at_ms": null, "completed_at_ms": null}, "item": {"type": "agentMessage", "id": "item-265", "text": "Voy a recuperar el esquema desde la copia DBML local y cargarlo en la pestaña de `dbdiagram.io` donde ya iniciaste sesión, sin abrir otra copia innecesaria.", "phase": "commentary", "memoryCitation": null, "delivery": null, "questions": null}}
{"record_type": "item", "metadata": {"thread_id": "019eb3a5-07e3-7163-a098-145f9d55e5f3", "turn_id": "019ef101-b04f-7f32-a359-1411515b670d", "item_id": "exec-f040259e-7905-43dc-b1b0-f2ab5094e493", "rollout_ordinal": 2251, "created_at_ms": 1782159910180, "item_type": "mcpToolCall", "updated_at_ordinal": 2251, "started_at_ms": null, "completed_at_ms": null}, "item": {"type": "mcpToolCall", "id": "exec-f040259e-7905-43dc-b1b0-f2ab5094e493", "server": "node_repl", "tool": "js", "status": "completed", "arguments": {"title": "Reconectar con dbdiagram.io", "code": "var { setupBrowserRuntime } = await import(\"C:/Users/Diego Tapia/.codex/plugins/cache/openai-bundled/browser/26.616.51431/scripts/browser-client.mjs\"); await setupBrowserRuntime({ globals: globalThis }); globalThis.browser = await agent.browsers.get(\"iab\"); nodeRepl.write(await browser.documentation());"}, "appContext": null, "mcpAppUi": null, "pluginId": null, "readOnlyHint": null, "result": {"content": [{"type": "text", "text": "## Additional Capabilities\n### Browser Capabilities\n- `visibility`: Use to show or hide the browser to the user, and to determine the browser's current visibility. Keep browser work in the background unless the user asks to see it or live viewing is useful. When the browser should be visible, call set(true).\n  Read with `await (await browser.capabilities.get(\"visibility\")).documentation()`.\n- `viewport`: Controls an explicit browser viewport override for responsive or device-size testing. Use it when a task calls for specific dimensions or breakpoint validation; otherwise leave it unset so the browser uses its normal 1280x720 viewport. Reset temporary overrides before finishing unless the user asked to keep them.\n  Read with `await (await browser.capabilities.get(\"viewport\")).documentation()`.\n### Tab Capabilities\n- `pageAssets`: List assets already observed in the current page state and bundle selected assets into a temporary local artifact.\n  Read with `await (await tab.capabilities.get(\"pageAssets\")).documentation()`.\n\n## Playwright\r\n\r\nPlaywright is a critical part of the JavaScript API available to you.\r\n\r\nYou only have access to a limited subset of the Playwright API, so only call functions that are explicitly defined.\r\nYou do have access to `tab.playwright.evaluate(...)`, but only in a read-only page scope.\r\nUse locators for scoped interactions and targeted checks. For bulk DOM inspection, prefer one bounded read-only `evaluate(...)` that queries and projects the needed data. Avoid loops of locator property calls. In `evaluate(...)`, use basic DOM reads, limit returned elements, and do not assume globals or helpers such as `performance`, `NodeFilter`, `document.createTreeWalker`, or `FormData` exist.\r\n\r\nWhen using Playwright, keep and reuse a recent `tab.playwright.domSnapshot()` when it is available and you need it for locator construction or retry decisions. Treat the latest relevant snapshot as the source of truth for locator construction and retry decisions.\r\n\r\n### Snapshot Discipline\r\n\r\n- Keep and reuse the latest relevant `domSnapshot()` until it proves stale or you need locator ground truth for UI that was not present in it.\r\n- Take a fresh `domSnapshot()` after navigation when you need to orient yourself or construct locators on the new page.\r\n- If a click times out, strict mode fails, or a selector parse error occurs, take a fresh `domSnapshot()` before forming the next locator.\r\n- Construct locators only from what appears in the latest snapshot. Do not guess labels, accessible names, or selectors.\r\n- Do not print full snapshot text repeatedly when a smaller excerpt, a `count()`, a specific attribute, or a direct locator check would answer the question with fewer tokens.\r\n- Do not discover page content by iterating through many results, cards, links, or rows and reading their text or attributes one by one.\r\n- Do not loop over a broad locator with `all()` and call `getAttribute(...)`, `textContent()`, or `innerText()` on each match. Each read crosses the browser boundary and becomes extremely expensive on large pages.\r\n- `locator.getAttribute(...)` is a single-element read, not a batch read. If the locator matches multiple elements, expect a strict-mode error rather than an array of attributes.\r\n- Use one broad observation to orient yourself: usually one fresh snapshot, or one screenshot if the visual structure is clearer than the DOM.\r\n- After that orientation step, narrow to the relevant section or a small number of strong candidates.\r\n- If the page is not getting narrower, do not scale up extraction across more elements. Change strategy instead.\r\n- Do not use `locator(...).allTextContents()`, `locator(\"body\").textContent()`, or `locator(\"body\").innerText()` as exploratory search tools across a page or large container.\r\n- Use broad text or attribute extraction only after you have already identified the exact container or element you need, and only when a smaller scoped check would not answer the question.\r\n- When you need many links, media URLs, or result titles, prefer a single `domSnapshot()` and parse the relevant lines, use the site's own search/filter UI, or navigate directly to a focused results page. Only fall back to per-element reads for a small, already-scoped set of candidates.\r\n- Do not use large body-text dumps, embedded app-state JSON such as `__NEXT_DATA__`, or repeated full-page extraction across multiple candidate pages as an exploratory search strategy.\r\n- Use large text or embedded JSON extraction only after you have already identified the relevant page, or when a site-specific skill explicitly depends on it.\r\n\r\n### Hard Constraints For Playwright In This Runtime\r\n\r\n- Do not pass a regex as `name` to `getByRole(...)` in this environment. Use a plain string `name` only.\r\n- Do not use `.first()`, `.last()`, or `.nth()` unless you have just called `count()` on the same locator and explicitly confirmed why that position is correct.\r\n- Do not click, fill, or press on a locator until you have verified it resolves to exactly one element when uniqueness is not obvious.\r\n- Do not retry the same failing locator without a fresh `domSnapshot()`.\r\n- Do not use a guessed locator as an exploratory probe. If the latest snapshot does not clearly support the locator, do not spend timeout budget testing it.\r\n- Do not assume browser-side Playwright supports the full upstream API surface. If a method is not explicitly known to exist, do not call it.\r\n- Do not assume `locator(...).selectOption(...)` exists in this environment.\r\n\r\n### Required Interaction Recipe\r\n\r\nBefore every click, fill, select-like action, or press:\r\n\r\n1. Reuse the latest relevant `domSnapshot()` when it still contains the locator ground truth you need. Take a fresh one only when it does not.\r\n2. Build the most stable locator from the latest snapshot.\r\n3. If uniqueness is not obvious from the selector itself, call `count()` on that locator.\r\n4. Proceed only if the locator resolves to exactly one element.\r\n5. Perform the action.\r\n6. After the action, collect another observation only when the next decision requires it. Prefer a targeted state check when it answers the question; take a fresh snapshot when you need new locator ground truth.\r\n\r\nIf `count()` is `0`:\r\n\r\n- The selector is wrong, stale, hidden, or the UI state is not ready.\r\n- Do not click anyway.\r\n- Do not wait on that locator to see if it eventually works.\r\n- Re-snapshot and rebuild the locator.\r\n\r\nIf `count()` is greater than `1`:\r\n\r\n- The selector is ambiguous.\r\n- Scope to the correct container or switch to a stronger attribute.\r\n- Do not use `.first()` as a shortcut.\r\n\r\n### Locator Strategy\r\n\r\nBuild locators from what the snapshot actually shows, not what looks visually obvious.\r\n\r\nPrefer the most stable contract, in this order:\r\n\r\n1. `data-testid`\r\n2. Stable `data-*` attributes\r\n3. Stable `href` (prefer exact or strong matches over broad substrings)\r\n4. Scoped semantic role + accessible name using a string `name`\r\n5. Scoped `getByText(...)`\r\n6. Scoped CSS selectors via `locator(...)`\r\n7. A scoped DOM-based click path or node-ID-based click when Playwright cannot produce a unique stable locator\r\n\r\nUse the most specific locator that is still durable.\r\n\r\nTreat a stable `href` as a strong hint, not proof of uniqueness. If multiple elements share the same `href`, scope to the correct card or container and confirm `count()` before clicking.\r\n\r\nTreat generic labels like `Menu`, `Main Menu`, `Help`, `Close`, `Default`, `Color`, `Size`, single-letter size labels such as `S`, `M`, `L`, `XL`, `Sort by`, `Search`, and `Add to cart` as ambiguous by default. Scope them to the correct container before acting.\r\n\r\nOn search results, product grids, carousels, and modal-heavy pages, repeated `href`s and repeated generic labels are ambiguous by default. First identify the stable card or container, then scope the locator inside that container before clicking.\r\n\r\n### Using `getByRole(..., { name })`\r\n\r\n- `name` is the accessible name, which may differ from visible text.\r\n- In the snapshot:\r\n  - `link \"X\"` usually reflects the accessible name.\r\n  - Nested text may be visible text only.\r\n- Use `getByRole` only when the accessible name is clearly present and likely unique in the latest snapshot.\r\n\r\n### Interaction Best Practices\r\n\r\n- Scope before acting: find the right container or section first, then target the child element.\r\n- If you call `count()` on a locator, store the result in a local variable and reuse it unless the DOM changes.\r\n- Match the locator to the actual element type shown in the snapshot (link vs button vs menuitem vs generic text).\r\n- Do not assume every click navigates. If opening a menu or filter, wait for the expected UI state, not page load.\r\n- Prefer structured local signals such as selected control state, visible confirmation text, modal contents, a specific line item, or URL parameters over scraping broad result sections or dumping large parts of the page.\r\n- Do not add explicit `timeoutMs` to routine `click`, `fill`, `check`, or `setChecked` calls unless you have a concrete reason the target is slow to become actionable.\r\n- Reserve explicit timeout values for navigation, state transitions, or other known slow operations.\r\n- If you already know the exact destination URL and no click-side effect matters, prefer `tab.goto(url)` over a brittle locator click.\r\n- Do not reacquire `tab` inside each `node_repl` call. Reuse the existing `tab` binding to save tokens and preserve state. Only reacquire or reassign it when you intentionally switch tabs, after a kernel reset, or after a failed call that did not create the binding.\r\n- Do not use fixed sleeps as a default waiting strategy. After an action, prefer a concrete state check or targeted wait. Take a fresh snapshot when you need new locator ground truth.\r\n- If a fixed delay is truly unavoidable for a known transition, keep it short and follow it immediately with a specific verification step.\r\n\r\n### Error Recovery\r\n\r\n- A strict mode violation means your locator is ambiguous.\r\n- Do not retry the same locator after a strict mode violation.\r\n- After strict mode fails, immediately inspect a fresh snapshot and rebuild the locator using tighter scope, a disambiguating container, or a stable attribute.\r\n- If a checkbox or radio exists but `check()` or `setChecked()` reports that it is hidden or did not change state, stop retrying the underlying input. Click its scoped visible associated `label[for]` or enclosing visible control once, then verify checked state.\r\n- A selector parse error means the locator syntax is invalid in this runtime.\r\n- Do not reuse the same locator form after a selector parse error.\r\n- A timeout usually means the target is missing, hidden, stale, offscreen, not yet rendered, or the selector is too broad.\r\n- Do not retry the same locator immediately after a timeout.\r\n- After a timeout, take a fresh snapshot, confirm the target still exists, and then either refine the locator or fall back to a more stable attribute.\r\n- If role or accessible-name targeting is unstable, fall back deliberately to a stable attribute (`data-*`, `href`, etc.), not brittle CSS structure.\r\n- If two locator attempts fail on the same target, stop escalating complexity on role or text locators. Switch to the most stable visible attribute from the snapshot or use a scoped DOM-based click path.\r\n\r\n### Fallback Guidance\r\n\r\n- Prefer stable `href` values copied from the snapshot over guessed URL patterns.\r\n- Prefer scoped attribute selectors over global text selectors.\r\n- Use `getByText(...)` only when role-based or attribute-based locators are not reliable, and scope it to a container whenever possible.\r\n- Prefer attributes copied directly from the latest snapshot over inferred semantics, fragile CSS chains, or positional selectors.\r\n- Do not invent likely selectors. If the snapshot does not clearly expose a unique target, fetch a fresh snapshot and reassess before acting.\n\n\n## API Reference\nUse this as the supported `agent.browsers.*` surface.\n\n```ts\n// Installed by setupBrowserRuntime({ globals: globalThis }).\nconst browser = await agent.browsers.get(\"iab\");\ninterface Agent {\n  browsers: Browsers; // API for finding and selecting browsers.\n  documentation: Documentation; // API for reading packaged browser-use documentation by name.\n}\n\ninterface Browsers {\n  get(id: string): Promise<Browser>; // Get a browser by id or client type.\n  list(): Promise<Array<{ capabilities: { browser?: Array<{ description: string; id: string }>; tab?: Array<{ description: string; id: string }> }; id: string; metadata?: Record<string, string>; name: string; type: \"iab\" | \"extension\" | \"cdp\" }>>; // List available browsers.\n}\n\ninterface Browser {\n  browserId: string; // Browser id selected by `agent.browsers.get()`.\n  capabilities: BrowserCapabilityCollection; // Browser-scoped optional capabilities advertised by the connected backend; discover IDs with `await browser.capabilities.list()`, then call `await (await browser.capabilities.get(id)).documentation()` for method details.\n  tabs: Tabs; // API for interacting with browser tabs.\n  user: BrowserUser; // Readonly context about tabs in the user's browser windows.\n  documentation(): Promise<string>; // Read browser guidance and the core API reference.\n  nameSession(name: string): Promise<void>; // Name the current browser automation session.\n}\n\ninterface BrowserUser {\n  claimTab(tab: string | BrowserUserTabInfo): Promise<Tab>; // Claim a user tab returned by `openTabs()` and return it as a controllable agent tab.\n\n  openTabs(): Promise<Array<BrowserUserTabInfo>>; // List open top-level tabs across the user's browser windows ordered by `lastOpened` descending.\n}\n\ninterface Tabs {\n\n  finalize(options: FinalizeTabsOptions): Promise<void>; // Finalize the browser session's tabs by cleaning up tabs that are no longer needed.\n  get(id: string): Promise<Tab>; // Get a tab by id.\n  list(): Promise<Array<TabInfo>>; // List open tabs in the browser.\n  new(): Promise<Tab>; // Create and return a new tab in the browser.\n  selected(): Promise<undefined | Tab>; // Return the currently selected tab, if any.\n}\n\ninterface Tab {\n  capabilities: TabCapabilityCollection; // Tab-scoped optional capabilities advertised by the connected backend; discover IDs with `await tab.capabilities.list()`, then call `await (await tab.capabilities.get(id)).documentation()` for method details.\n  clipboard: TabClipboardAPI; // API for interacting with the browser session's clipboard.\n\n  cua: CUAAPI; // API for interacting with the tab via the cua api\n  dev: TabDevAPI; // API for developer-oriented tab inspection.\n  dom_cua: DomCUAAPI; // API for interacting with the tab via the dom based cua api\n  id: string; // A tab's unique identifier\n  playwright: PlaywrightAPI; // API for interacting with the tab via the playwright api\n  back(): Promise<void>; // Navigate this tab back in history.\n  close(): Promise<void>; // Close this tab.\n  forward(): Promise<void>; // Navigate this tab forward in history.\n  getJsDialog(): Promise<undefined | Dialog>; // Get the active JavaScript dialog for this tab, if one is currently open.\n  goto(url: string): Promise<void>; // Open a URL in this tab.\n  reload(): Promise<void>; // Reload this tab.\n  screenshot(options: ScreenshotOptions): Promise<Uint8Array>; // Capture a screenshot of this tab.\n  title(): Promise<undefined | string>; // Get the current title for this tab.\n  url(): Promise<undefined | string>; // Get the current URL for this tab.\n}\n\ninterface CUAAPI {\n  click(options: ClickOptions): Promise<void>; // Click at a coordinate in the current viewport.\n  double_click(options: DoubleClickOptions): Promise<void>; // Double click at a coordinate in the current viewport.\n  \n  drag(options: DragOptions): Promise<void>; // Drag from a point to a point by the provided path.\n  keypress(options: KeypressOptions): Promise<void>; // Press control characters at the current focused element (focus it first via click/dblclick).\n  move(options: MoveOptions): Promise<void>; // Move the mouse to a point by the provided x and y coordinates.\n  scroll(options: ScrollOptions): Promise<void>; // Scroll by a delta from a specific viewport coordinate.\n  type(options: TypeOptions): Promise<void>; // Type text at the current focus.\n}\n\ninterface DomCUAAPI {\n  click(options: DomClickOptions): Promise<void>; // Click a DOM node by its id from the visible DOM snapshot.\n  double_click(options: DomClickOptions): Promise<void>; // Double-click a DOM node by its id.\n  \n  get_visible_dom(): Promise<unknown>; // Return a filtered DOM with node ids for interactable elements.\n  keypress(options: DomKeypressOptions): Promise<void>; // Press control characters at the currently focused element (focus it first via click/dblclick).\n  scroll(options: DomScrollOptions): Promise<void>; // Scroll either the page or a specific node (if node_id provided) by deltas.\n  type(options: DomTypeOptions): Promise<void>; // Type text into the currently focused element (focus via click first).\n}\n\ninterface PlaywrightAPI {\n  domSnapshot(): Promise<string>; // Return a snapshot of the current DOM as a string, including expanded iframe body content when available.\n\n  evaluate<TResult, TArg>(pageFunction: PlaywrightEvaluateFunction<TArg, TResult>, arg?: TArg, options?: PlaywrightEvaluateOptions): Promise<TResult>; // Evaluate JavaScript in a read-only page scope.\n  expectNavigation<T>(action: () => Promise<T>, options: { timeoutMs?: number; url?: string; waitUntil?: LoadState }): Promise<T>; // Expect a navigation triggered by an action.\n  frameLocator(frameSelector: string): PlaywrightFrameLocator; // Create a frame-scoped locator builder.\n  getByLabel(text: TextMatcher, options: { exact?: boolean }): PlaywrightLocator; // Find elements by label text within the page.\n  getByPlaceholder(text: TextMatcher, options: { exact?: boolean }): PlaywrightLocator; // Find elements by placeholder text within the page.\n  getByRole(role: string, options: { exact?: boolean; name?: TextMatcher }): PlaywrightLocator; // Find elements by ARIA role within the page.\n  getByTestId(testId: string): PlaywrightLocator; // Find elements by test id within the page.\n  getByText(text: TextMatcher, options: { exact?: boolean }): PlaywrightLocator; // Find elements by text within the page.\n  locator(selector: string): PlaywrightLocator; // Create a locator scoped to this tab.\n  waitForEvent(event: \"download\", options?: WaitForEventOptions): Promise<PlaywrightDownload>; // Wait for the next event on the page.\n\n  waitForLoadState(options: PageWaitForLoadStateOptions): Promise<void>; // Wait for the page to reach a specific load state.\n  waitForTimeout(timeoutMs: number): Promise<void>; // Wait for a fixed duration.\n  waitForURL(url: string, options: PageWaitForURLOptions): Promise<void>; // Wait for the page URL to match the provided value.\n}\n\ninterface PlaywrightFrameLocator {\n  frameLocator(frameSelector: string): PlaywrightFrameLocator; // Create a locator scoped to a nested frame.\n  getByLabel(text: TextMatcher, options: { exact?: boolean }): PlaywrightLocator; // Find elements by label within this frame.\n  getByPlaceholder(text: TextMatcher, options: { exact?: boolean }): PlaywrightLocator; // Find elements by placeholder within this frame.\n  getByRole(role: string, options: { exact?: boolean; name?: TextMatcher }): PlaywrightLocator; // Find elements by ARIA role within this frame.\n  getByTestId(testId: string): PlaywrightLocator; // Find elements by test id within this frame.\n  getByText(text: TextMatcher, options: { exact?: boolean }): PlaywrightLocator; // Find elements by text within this frame.\n  locator(selector: string): PlaywrightLocator; // Create a locator scoped to this frame.\n}\n\ninterface PlaywrightLocator {\n  all(): Promise<Array<PlaywrightLocator>>; // Resolve to a list of locators for each matched element.\n  allTextContents(options: { timeoutMs?: number }): Promise<Array<string>>; // Return `textContent` for *all* elements matched by this locator.\n  and(locator: PlaywrightLocator): PlaywrightLocator; // Return a locator matching elements that satisfy both this locator and `locator`.\n  check(options: LocatorCheckOptions): Promise<void>; // Check a checkbox or switch-like control.\n  click(options: LocatorClickOptions): Promise<void>; // Click the element matched by this locator.\n  count(): Promise<number>; // Number of elements matching this locator.\n  dblclick(options: LocatorClickOptions): Promise<void>; // Double-click the element matched by this locator.\n  downloadMedia(options: LocatorDownloadMediaOptions): Promise<void>; // Trigger a media download for the first matched element.\n  fill(value: string, options: { timeoutMs?: number }): Promise<void>; // Replace the element's value with the provided text.\n  filter(options: LocatorFilterOptions): PlaywrightLocator; // Narrow this locator by additional constraints.\n  first(): PlaywrightLocator; // Return a locator pointing at the first matched element.\n  getAttribute(name: string, options: { timeoutMs?: number }): Promise<null | string>; // Return an attribute value from the first matched element.\n  getByLabel(text: TextMatcher, options: { exact?: boolean }): PlaywrightLocator; // Find elements by label text, scoped to this locator.\n  getByPlaceholder(text: TextMatcher, options: { exact?: boolean }): PlaywrightLocator; // Find elements by placeholder text, scoped to this locator.\n  getByRole(role: string, options: { exact?: boolean; name?: TextMatcher }): PlaywrightLocator; // Find elements by ARIA role, scoped to this locator.\n  getByTestId(testId: string): PlaywrightLocator; // Find elements by test id, scoped to this locator.\n  getByText(text: TextMatcher, options: { exact?: boolean }): PlaywrightLocator; // Find elements by text content, scoped to this locator.\n  innerText(options: { timeoutMs?: number }): Promise<string>; // Return the rendered (visible) text of the first matched element.\n  isEnabled(): Promise<boolean>; // Whether the first matched element is currently enabled.\n  isVisible(): Promise<boolean>; // Whether the first matched element is currently visible.\n  last(): PlaywrightLocator; // Return a locator pointing at the last matched element.\n  locator(selector: string, options: LocatorLocatorOptions): PlaywrightLocator; // Create a descendant locator scoped to this locator.\n  nth(index: number): PlaywrightLocator; // Return a locator pointing at the Nth matched element.\n  or(locator: PlaywrightLocator): PlaywrightLocator; // Return a locator matching elements that satisfy either this locator or `locator`.\n  press(value: string, options: { timeoutMs?: number }): Promise<void>; // Press a keyboard key while this locator is focused.\n  selectOption(value: SelectOptionInput | Array<SelectOptionInput>, options: { timeoutMs?: number }): Promise<void>; // Select one or more options on a native `<select>` element.\n  setChecked(checked: boolean, options: LocatorCheckOptions): Promise<void>; // Set a checkbox or switch-like control to a checked/unchecked state.\n  textContent(options: { timeoutMs?: number }): Promise<null | string>; // Return the raw textContent of the first matched element (or null if missing).\n  type(value: string, options: { timeoutMs?: number }): Promise<void>; // Type text into the element without clearing existing content.\n  uncheck(options: LocatorCheckOptions): Promise<void>; // Uncheck a checkbox or switch-like control.\n  waitFor(options: LocatorWaitForOptions): Promise<void>; // Wait for the element to reach a specific state.\n}\n\ninterface PlaywrightDownload {\n\n}\n\ninterface TabClipboardAPI {\n  read(): Promise<Array<TabClipboardItem>>; // Read clipboard items, including text and binary payloads.\n  readText(): Promise<string>; // Read plain text from the browser clipboard.\n  write(items: Array<TabClipboardItem>): Promise<void>; // Write clipboard items.\n  writeText(text: string): Promise<void>; // Write plain text to the browser clipboard.\n}\n\ninterface TabDevAPI {\n  logs(options: TabDevLogsOptions): Promise<Array<TabDevLogEntry>>; // Read console log messages captured for this tab.\n}\n\ninterface AlertDialog {\n  type: \"alert\";\n  dismiss(): Promise<void>;\n}\n\ninterface BeforeUnloadDialog {\n  type: \"beforeunload\";\n  dismiss(): Promise<void>;\n}\n\ninterface ConfirmDialog {\n  type: \"confirm\";\n  accept(): Promise<void>;\n  dismiss(): Promise<void>;\n}\n\ninterface Documentation {\n  get(name: string): Promise<string>; // Read packaged documentation by its extensionless relative path.\n}\n\ninterface PromptDialog {\n  type: \"prompt\";\n  accept(text: string): Promise<void>;\n  dismiss(): Promise<void>;\n}\n\ntype BrowserCapabilityCollection = {\n  get(id: string): Promise<unknown>;\n  list(): Promise<Array<{ id: string; description: string }>>;\n};\n\ninterface BrowserUserTabInfo {\n  id: string; // Opaque identifier for this browser tab.\n  lastOpened?: string; // ISO 8601 timestamp for the last time the tab was opened or focused.\n  tabGroup?: string; // User-visible tab group name when the tab belongs to one.\n  title?: string; // User-visible tab title.\n  url?: string; // Current tab URL.\n}\n\ninterface TabsContentOptions {\n\n  timeoutMs?: number; // Maximum time to wait for each page load, in milliseconds.\n  urls: Array<string>; // URLs to load in temporary background tabs.\n}\n\ninterface TabsContentResult {\n\n  title: null | string; // The resolved page title when available.\n  url: string; // The resolved page URL when available, otherwise the requested URL.\n}\n\ninterface FinalizeTabsOptions {\n  keep?: Array<FinalizeTabsKeep>; // Explicit tab dispositions to preserve after cleanup.\n}\n\ninterface TabInfo {\n  id: string; // Metadata describing an open tab.\n  title?: string;\n  url?: string;\n}\n\ntype TabCapabilityCollection = {\n  get(id: string): Promise<unknown>;\n  list(): Promise<Array<{ id: string; description: string }>>;\n};\n\ntype Dialog = AlertDialog | BeforeUnloadDialog | ConfirmDialog | PromptDialog;\n\ntype ScreenshotOptions = {\n  clip?: ClipRect; // Crop to a specific rectangle instead of the full viewport.\n  fullPage?: boolean; // Capture the full page instead of the viewport.\n};\n\ntype ClickOptions = {\n  button?: number; // Mouse button (1-left, 2-middle/wheel, 3-right, 4-back, 5-forward).\n  keypress?: Array<string>; // Modifier keys held during the click.\n  x: number;\n  y: number;\n};\n\ntype DoubleClickOptions = {\n  keypress?: Array<string>; // Modifier keys held during the double click.\n  x: number;\n  y: number;\n};\n\ntype DragOptions = {\n  keys?: Array<string>; // Optional modifier keys held during the drag.\n  path: Array<{ x: number; y: number }>; // Drag path as a list of points.\n};\n\ntype KeypressOptions = {\n  keys: Array<string>; // Key combination to press.\n};\n\ntype MoveOptions = {\n  keys?: Array<string>; // Optional modifier keys held while moving.\n  x: number;\n  y: number;\n};\n\ntype ScrollOptions = {\n  keypress?: Array<string>; // Modifier keys held during scroll.\n  scrollX: number;\n  scrollY: number;\n  x: number;\n  y: number;\n};\n\ntype TypeOptions = {\n  text: string;\n};\n\ntype DomClickOptions = {\n  node_id: string; // Node id from `get_visible_dom()`.\n};\n\ntype DomKeypressOptions = {\n  keys: Array<string>; // Key combination to press.\n};\n\ntype DomScrollOptions = {\n  node_id?: string; // Optional node id to scroll within.\n  x: number; // Horizontal scroll delta.\n  y: number; // Vertical scroll delta.\n};\n\ntype DomTypeOptions = {\n  text: string; // Text to type into the currently focused element.\n};\n\ntype ElementInfoOptions = {\n  includeNonInteractable?: boolean; // When true, include non-interactable elements in addition to interactable targets.\n  x: number;\n  y: number;\n};\n\ntype ElementInfo = {\n  ariaName?: string | null; // Accessible name if available.\n  boundingBox?: ElementInfoRect | null; // Element bounds in screenshot coordinates.\n  nodeId?: number | null; // Backend node id that can be passed to DOM-inspection APIs when available.\n  preview: string; // Compact human-readable node preview.\n  role?: string | null; // Computed ARIA role if available.\n  selector: ElementInfoSelector; // Suggested selector data for this element.\n  tagName: string; // Lowercased HTML tag name.\n  testId?: string | null; // Configured test id attribute if present.\n  visibleText?: string | null; // Rendered visible text, selected option text, or visible form value when available.\n};\n\ntype ElementScreenshotOptions = {\n  includeNonInteractable?: boolean; // When true, highlight non-interactable elements in addition to interactable targets.\n  x: number;\n  y: number;\n};\n\ntype PlaywrightEvaluateFunction<TArg, TResult> = string | (arg: TArg) => TResult | Promise<TResult>;\n\ntype PlaywrightEvaluateOptions = {\n  timeoutMs?: number; // Maximum time to spend setting up the read-only DOM scope and running the script.\n};\n\ntype LoadState = \"load\" | \"domcontentloaded\" | \"networkidle\";\n\ntype TextMatcher = string | RegExp;\n\ntype WaitForEventOptions = {\n  timeoutMs?: number;\n};\n\ntype PageWaitForLoadStateOptions = {\n  state?: LoadState;\n  timeoutMs?: number;\n};\n\ntype PageWaitForURLOptions = {\n  timeoutMs?: number;\n  waitUntil?: WaitUntil;\n};\n\ntype LocatorCheckOptions = {\n  force?: boolean;\n  timeoutMs?: number;\n};\n\ntype LocatorClickOptions = {\n  button?: MouseButton;\n  force?: boolean;\n  modifiers?: Array<KeyboardModifier>;\n  timeoutMs?: number;\n};\n\ntype LocatorDownloadMediaOptions = {\n  timeoutMs?: number;\n};\n\ntype LocatorFilterOptions = {\n  has?: PlaywrightLocator;\n  hasNot?: PlaywrightLocator;\n  hasNotText?: TextMatcher;\n  hasText?: TextMatcher;\n  visible?: boolean;\n};\n\ntype LocatorLocatorOptions = {\n  has?: PlaywrightLocator;\n  hasNot?: PlaywrightLocator;\n  hasNotText?: TextMatcher;\n  hasText?: TextMatcher;\n};\n\ntype SelectOptionInput = string | SelectOptionDescriptor;\n\ntype LocatorWaitForOptions = {\n  state: WaitForState;\n  timeoutMs?: number;\n};\n\ntype TabClipboardItem = {\n  entries: Array<TabClipboardEntry>;\n  presentationStyle?: \"unspecified\" | \"inline\" | \"attachment\";\n};\n\ninterface TabDevLogsOptions {\n  filter?: string; // Optional substring filter applied to the rendered log message.\n  levels?: Array<\"debug\" | \"info\" | \"log\" | \"warn\" | \"error\" | \"warning\">; // Optional levels to include.\n  limit?: number; // Maximum number of logs to return.\n}\n\ninterface TabDevLogEntry {\n  level: \"debug\" | \"info\" | \"log\" | \"warn\" | \"error\"; // Console log level.\n  message: string; // Rendered log message text.\n  timestamp: string; // ISO 8601 timestamp for when the runtime captured the log.\n  url?: string; // Source URL reported by the browser runtime, when available.\n}\n\ntype TabsContentType = \"html\" | \"text\" | \"domSnapshot\";\n\ninterface FinalizeTabsKeep {\n  status: FinalizeTabStatus; // Where the kept tab belongs after cleanup.\n  tab: string | Tab | TabInfo; // Tab object to keep open after browser cleanup.\n}\n\ntype ClipRect = {\n  height: number;\n  width: number;\n  x: number;\n  y: number;\n};\n\ntype ElementInfoRect = {\n  height: number;\n  width: number;\n  x: number;\n  y: number;\n};\n\ntype ElementInfoSelector = {\n  candidates: Array<string>; // Ranked selector candidates for the element.\n  frameSelectors?: Array<string>; // Frame selectors to enter before using the element selector.\n  primary?: string | null; // The preferred selector for the element when available.\n};\n\ntype WaitUntil = LoadState | \"commit\";\n\ntype MouseButton = \"left\" | \"right\" | \"middle\";\n\ntype KeyboardModifier = \"Alt\" | \"Control\" | \"ControlOrMeta\" | \"Meta\" | \"Shift\";\n\ntype SelectOptionDescriptor = {\n  index?: number;\n  label?: string;\n  value?: string;\n};\n\ntype WaitForState = \"attached\" | \"detached\" | \"visible\" | \"hidden\";\n\ntype TabClipboardEntry = {\n  base64?: string;\n  mimeType: string;\n  text?: string;\n};\n\ntype FinalizeTabStatus = \"handoff\" | \"deliverable\";\n```\n"}], "structuredContent": null, "_meta": {"browser_use": {}, "codex/toolSurface": {"backend": "iab", "kind": "browserUse"}}}, "error": null, "durationMs": 85}}
{"record_type": "item", "metadata": {"thread_id": "019eb3a5-07e3-7163-a098-145f9d55e5f3", "turn_id": "019ef101-b04f-7f32-a359-1411515b670d", "item_id": "exec-bbd5fd6a-722a-4a3d-9af9-3a26c7b7952e", "rollout_ordinal": 2256, "created_at_ms": 1782159922891, "item_type": "mcpToolCall", "updated_at_ordinal": 2256, "started_at_ms": null, "completed_at_ms": null}, "item": {"type": "mcpToolCall", "id": "exec-bbd5fd6a-722a-4a3d-9af9-3a26c7b7952e", "server": "node_repl", "tool": "js", "status": "completed", "arguments": {"title": "Encontrar la pestaña iniciada", "code": "var openUserTabs = await browser.user.openTabs(); nodeRepl.write(JSON.stringify(openUserTabs));"}, "appContext": null, "mcpAppUi": null, "pluginId": null, "readOnlyHint": null, "result": {"content": [{"type": "text", "text": "[{\"id\":\"2\",\"title\":\"No se puede acceder a este sitio\",\"url\":\"http://localhost:11434/\"},{\"id\":\"3\",\"title\":\"Modelo de datos - Tesis Karaoke - dbdiagram.io\",\"url\":\"https://dbdiagram.io/d/Modelo-de-datos-Tesis-Karaoke-6a3999ad9340ecc065f0ce55\"},{\"id\":\"4\",\"title\":\"Sign in to dbdiagram\",\"url\":\"https://dbdiagram.io\"}]"}], "structuredContent": null, "_meta": {"browser_use": {}, "codex/toolSurface": {"backend": "iab", "kind": "browserUse"}}}, "error": null, "durationMs": 9}}
{"record_type": "item", "metadata": {"thread_id": "019eb3a5-07e3-7163-a098-145f9d55e5f3", "turn_id": "019ef101-b04f-7f32-a359-1411515b670d", "item_id": "exec-4d266ef2-4c59-4e05-ad3a-4819da42ab57", "rollout_ordinal": 2261, "created_at_ms": 1782159938487, "item_type": "mcpToolCall", "updated_at_ordinal": 2261, "started_at_ms": null, "completed_at_ms": null}, "item": {"type": "mcpToolCall", "id": "exec-4d266ef2-4c59-4e05-ad3a-4819da42ab57", "server": "node_repl", "tool": "js", "status": "completed", "arguments": {"title": "Recuperar el diagrama existente", "code": "var modelInfo = openUserTabs.find(t=>t.url.includes(\"/d/Modelo-de-datos-Tesis-Karaoke\")); if(!modelInfo) throw new Error(\"No se encontró la pestaña del modelo\"); var modelTab = await browser.user.claimTab(modelInfo); await (await browser.capabilities.get(\"visibility\")).set(true); nodeRepl.write(JSON.stringify({url:await modelTab.url(),title:await modelTab.title()}));"}, "appContext": null, "mcpAppUi": null, "pluginId": null, "readOnlyHint": null, "result": {"content": [{"type": "text", "text": "{\"url\":\"https://dbdiagram.io/d/Modelo-de-datos-Tesis-Karaoke-6a3999ad9340ecc065f0ce55\",\"title\":\"Modelo de datos - Tesis Karaoke - dbdiagram.io\"}"}], "structuredContent": null, "_meta": {"browser_use": {}, "codex/toolSurface": {"backend": "iab", "kind": "browserUse"}}}, "error": null, "durationMs": 320}}
{"record_type": "item", "metadata": {"thread_id": "019eb3a5-07e3-7163-a098-145f9d55e5f3", "turn_id": "019ef101-b04f-7f32-a359-1411515b670d", "item_id": "exec-62a113d9-9404-4bd2-b1df-a814d240c9ef", "rollout_ordinal": 2266, "created_at_ms": 1782159958556, "item_type": "mcpToolCall", "updated_at_ordinal": 2266, "started_at_ms": null, "completed_at_ms": null}, "item": {"type": "mcpToolCall", "id": "exec-62a113d9-9404-4bd2-b1df-a814d240c9ef", "server": "node_repl", "tool": "js", "status": "completed", "arguments": {"title": "Verificar el diagrama recuperado", "code": "nodeRepl.write(await modelTab.playwright.domSnapshot());"}, "appContext": null, "mcpAppUi": null, "pluginId": null, "readOnlyHint": null, "result": {"content": [{"type": "text", "text": "- banner:\n  - button \"dbdiagram-logo Personal\":\n    - img \"dbdiagram-logo\"\n    - generic: Personal\n  - generic: /\n  - img \"saved\"\n  - textbox:\n    - /placeholder: Untitled Diagram\n    - text: Modelo de datos - Tesis Karaoke\n  - button:\n- code:\n  - generic: \"145\"\n  - generic: \"146\"\n  - generic: \"147\"\n  - generic: \"148\"\n  - generic: \"149\"\n  - generic: \"150\"\n  - generic: \n  - generic: \"151\"\n  - generic: \"152\"\n  - generic: \"153\"\n  - generic: \"154\"\n  - generic: \"155\"\n  - generic: \"156\"\n  - generic: \n  - generic: \"157\"\n  - generic: \"158\"\n  - generic: \"159\"\n  - generic: \"160\"\n  - generic: \"161\"\n  - generic: \"162\"\n  - generic: \"163\"\n  - generic: \n  - generic: \"164\"\n  - generic: \"165\"\n  - generic: \"Ref: retroalimentacion_segmento.retroalimentacion_id > retroalimentacion.id\"\n  - generic: \"Ref: retroalimentacion_segmento.segmento_id > segmento.id\"\n  - generic: \"Ref: comparacion.analisis_anterior_id > analisis.id\"\n  - generic: \"Ref: comparacion.analisis_actual_id > analisis.id\"\n  - generic: \"Ref: cambio.comparacion_id > comparacion.id\"\n  - generic: \"TableGroup Preparacion {\"\n  - generic: cancion\n  - generic: referencia\n  - generic: configuracion\n  - generic: \"}\"\n  - generic: \"TableGroup Sesiones_y_analisis {\"\n  - generic: sesion\n  - generic: analisis\n  - generic: metrica\n  - generic: segmento\n  - generic: \"}\"\n  - generic: \"TableGroup Retroalimentacion_y_evolucion {\"\n  - generic: retroalimentacion\n  - textbox \"Editor content;Press Alt+F1 for Accessibility Options.\": \"segmento } TableGroup Retroalimentacion_y_evolucion { retroalimentacion retroalimentacion_segmento comparacion cambio } // Use DBML to define your database structure\"\n- link \"banner image 🔥 Embed Dashboards In 15 Minutes 🔥 Fast, flexible, and pixel-perfect embedded analytics is just a snippet away.\":\n  - /url: https://www.holistics.io/product/embedded-analytics/?utm_source=dbdiagram&utm_medium=ads\n  - img \"banner image\"\n  - generic: 🔥 Embed Dashboards In 15 Minutes 🔥\n  - paragraph: Fast, flexible, and pixel-perfect embedded analytics is just a snippet away.\n- button:\n- generic: 8%\n- button:\n- button \"1\":\n  - generic: \"1\"\n- button:\n- button:\n- generic: \"2\"\n- button \"3\":\n  - generic: \"3\"\n- button \"4\":\n  - generic: \"4\"\n- button \"5 PRO\":\n  - generic: \"5\"\n  - generic: PRO\n- 'button \"Detail level: PRO\"':\n  - generic: \"Detail level:\"\n  - generic: PRO\n- generic: \"6\"\n- button:\n- button:\n- alert\n- alert\n- complementary\n- complementary"}], "structuredContent": null, "_meta": {"browser_use": {"url": "https://dbdiagram.io/d/Modelo-de-datos-Tesis-Karaoke-6a3999ad9340ecc065f0ce55"}, "codex/toolSurface": {"backend": "iab", "kind": "browserUse"}}}, "error": null, "durationMs": 344}}
{"record_type": "item", "metadata": {"thread_id": "019eb3a5-07e3-7163-a098-145f9d55e5f3", "turn_id": "019ef101-b04f-7f32-a359-1411515b670d", "item_id": "item-266", "rollout_ordinal": 2270, "created_at_ms": 1782159973037, "item_type": "agentMessage", "updated_at_ordinal": 2270, "started_at_ms": null, "completed_at_ms": null}, "item": {"type": "agentMessage", "id": "item-266", "text": "Lo recuperé: el diagrama sí quedó guardado en tu cuenta y tiene una URL permanente. Dejaré abierta esa pestaña y te entregaré también el enlace directo.", "phase": "commentary", "memoryCitation": null, "delivery": null, "questions": null}}
{"record_type": "item", "metadata": {"thread_id": "019eb3a5-07e3-7163-a098-145f9d55e5f3", "turn_id": "019ef101-b04f-7f32-a359-1411515b670d", "item_id": "exec-ebf6e4b9-d007-480c-b104-fe9f4bc3b810", "rollout_ordinal": 2273, "created_at_ms": 1782159976468, "item_type": "mcpToolCall", "updated_at_ordinal": 2273, "started_at_ms": null, "completed_at_ms": null}, "item": {"type": "mcpToolCall", "id": "exec-ebf6e4b9-d007-480c-b104-fe9f4bc3b810", "server": "node_repl", "tool": "js", "status": "completed", "arguments": {"title": "Dejar abierto el modelo recuperado", "code": "await browser.tabs.finalize({keep:[{tab:modelTab,status:\"deliverable\"}]}); nodeRepl.write(\"finalized\");"}, "appContext": null, "mcpAppUi": null, "pluginId": null, "readOnlyHint": null, "result": {"content": [{"type": "text", "text": "finalized"}], "structuredContent": null, "_meta": {"browser_use": {}, "codex/toolSurface": {"backend": "iab", "kind": "browserUse"}}}, "error": null, "durationMs": 15}}
{"record_type": "item", "metadata": {"thread_id": "019eb3a5-07e3-7163-a098-145f9d55e5f3", "turn_id": "019ef101-b04f-7f32-a359-1411515b670d", "item_id": "item-267", "rollout_ordinal": 2277, "created_at_ms": 1782159992187, "item_type": "agentMessage", "updated_at_ordinal": 2277, "started_at_ms": null, "completed_at_ms": null}, "item": {"type": "agentMessage", "id": "item-267", "text": "El diagrama estaba guardado. Enlace permanente:\n\n[Modelo de datos - Tesis Karaoke](https://dbdiagram.io/d/Modelo-de-datos-Tesis-Karaoke-6a3999ad9340ecc065f0ce55)\n\nTambién dejé abierta su pestaña y se conserva la copia [DBML local](<C:\\Users\\Diego Tapia\\Desktop\\Pene\\U\\Tesis\\tesis_karaoke\\docs\\modelo_datos_tesis.dbml>).", "phase": "final_answer", "memoryCitation": null, "delivery": null, "questions": null}}
{"record_type": "item", "metadata": {"thread_id": "019eb3a5-07e3-7163-a098-145f9d55e5f3", "turn_id": "019ef107-a69c-7682-bf58-602ad0cd4660", "item_id": "item-268", "rollout_ordinal": 2284, "created_at_ms": 1782160271097, "item_type": "userMessage", "updated_at_ordinal": 2284, "started_at_ms": null, "completed_at_ms": null}, "item": {"type": "userMessage", "id": "item-268", "clientId": "fd43f692-fec9-435b-94f5-e1a14c180c5d", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "\n# In app browser:\n- The user has the in-app browser open with 3 tabs.\n- Current URL: https://dbdiagram.io/d/Modelo-de-datos-Tesis-Karaoke-6a3999ad9340ecc065f0ce55\n\n## My request for Codex:\ncrea un documento con las referencias que quedaron en el documento final\n", "text_elements": []}]}}
{"record_type": "item", "metadata": {"thread_id": "019eb3a5-07e3-7163-a098-145f9d55e5f3", "turn_id": "019ef107-a69c-7682-bf58-602ad0cd4660", "item_id": "item-269", "rollout_ordinal": 2286, "created_at_ms": 1782160287083, "item_type": "agentMessage", "updated_at_ordinal": 2286, "started_at_ms": null, "completed_at_ms": null}, "item": {"type": "agentMessage", "id": "item-269", "text": "Voy a consolidar en un Word la bibliografía utilizada en los capítulos finales, eliminando duplicados y conservando la numeración que ya aparece en el texto. Primero revisaré los documentos generados para no incluir fuentes descartadas.", "phase": "commentary", "memoryCitation": null, "delivery": null, "questions": null}}
{"record_type": "item", "metadata": {"thread_id": "019eb3a5-07e3-7163-a098-145f9d55e5f3", "turn_id": "019ef107-a69c-7682-bf58-602ad0cd4660", "item_id": "item-270", "rollout_ordinal": 2300, "created_at_ms": 1782160350704, "item_type": "agentMessage", "updated_at_ordinal": 2300, "started_at_ms": null, "completed_at_ms": null}, "item": {"type": "agentMessage", "id": "item-270", "text": "Las versiones finales actuales contienen referencias confirmadas desde [5] hasta [30]; las [11], [13] y [16] se repiten en el capítulo 4, así que las consolidaré una sola vez. Prepararé el Word con numeración continua, sangría francesa y enlaces clicables.", "phase": "commentary", "memoryCitation": null, "delivery": null, "questions": null}}
{"record_type": "item", "metadata": {"thread_id": "019eb3a5-07e3-7163-a098-145f9d55e5f3", "turn_id": "019ef107-a69c-7682-bf58-602ad0cd4660", "item_id": "exec-40404445-12ab-4be6-b377-f9525e7faf5d", "rollout_ordinal": 2303, "created_at_ms": 1782160391255, "item_type": "fileChange", "updated_at_ordinal": 2303, "started_at_ms": null, "completed_at_ms": null}, "item": {"type": "fileChange", "id": "exec-40404445-12ab-4be6-b377-f9525e7faf5d", "changes": [{"path": "C:\\Users\\Diego Tapia\\Desktop\\Pene\\U\\Tesis\\tesis_karaoke\\docs\\generar_referencias_finales.py", "kind": {"type": "add"}, "diff": "import re\nfrom pathlib import Path\n\nfrom docx import Document\nfrom docx.enum.text import WD_ALIGN_PARAGRAPH\nfrom docx.oxml import OxmlElement\nfrom docx.oxml.ns import qn\nfrom docx.shared import Cm, Pt, RGBColor\n\n\nROOT = Path(__file__).resolve().parents[1]\nSOURCES = [\n    ROOT / \"Capitulo_2_Marco_teorico_actualizado.docx\",\n    ROOT / \"Capitulo_3_Metodologia_version_especifica.docx\",\n    ROOT / \"Capitulo_4_Desarrollo_version_especifica.docx\",\n]\nOUTPUT = ROOT / \"Referencias_documento_final.docx\"\nREFERENCE_RE = re.compile(r\"^\\[(\\d+)\\]\\s+(.+)$\")\nURL_RE = re.compile(r\"https?://\\S+\")\n\n\ndef format_run(run, size=12, bold=False):\n    run.font.name = \"Times New Roman\"\n    run._element.get_or_add_rPr().rFonts.set(qn(\"w:eastAsia\"), \"Times New Roman\")\n    run.font.size = Pt(size)\n    run.bold = bold\n\n\ndef add_hyperlink(paragraph, text, url):\n    relation_id = paragraph.part.relate_to(\n        url,\n        \"http://schemas.openxmlformats.org/officeDocument/2006/relationships/hyperlink\",\n        is_external=True,\n    )\n    hyperlink = OxmlElement(\"w:hyperlink\")\n    hyperlink.set(qn(\"r:id\"), relation_id)\n    run = OxmlElement(\"w:r\")\n    properties = OxmlElement(\"w:rPr\")\n    color = OxmlElement(\"w:color\")\n    color.set(qn(\"w:val\"), \"0563C1\")\n    underline = OxmlElement(\"w:u\")\n    underline.set(qn(\"w:val\"), \"single\")\n    fonts = OxmlElement(\"w:rFonts\")\n    fonts.set(qn(\"w:ascii\"), \"Times New Roman\")\n    fonts.set(qn(\"w:hAnsi\"), \"Times New Roman\")\n    size = OxmlElement(\"w:sz\")\n    size.set(qn(\"w:val\"), \"24\")\n    properties.extend([fonts, color, underline, size])\n    run.append(properties)\n    node = OxmlElement(\"w:t\")\n    node.text = text\n    run.append(node)\n    hyperlink.append(run)\n    paragraph._p.append(hyperlink)\n\n\ndef collect_references():\n    references = {}\n    for source in SOURCES:\n        document = Document(source)\n        for paragraph in document.paragraphs:\n            match = REFERENCE_RE.match(paragraph.text.strip())\n            if not match:\n                continue\n            number = int(match.group(1))\n            value = match.group(2).strip()\n            if number not in references or len(value) > len(references[number]):\n                references[number] = value\n    return references\n\n\ndef add_reference(document, number, value):\n    paragraph = document.add_paragraph()\n    paragraph.alignment = WD_ALIGN_PARAGRAPH.JUSTIFY\n    paragraph.paragraph_format.left_indent = Cm(0.9)\n    paragraph.paragraph_format.first_line_indent = Cm(-0.9)\n    paragraph.paragraph_format.line_spacing = 1.15\n    paragraph.paragraph_format.space_after = Pt(7)\n    prefix = paragraph.add_run(f\"[{number}] \")\n    format_run(prefix)\n\n    cursor = 0\n    for match in URL_RE.finditer(value):\n        before = value[cursor : match.start()]\n        if before:\n            run = paragraph.add_run(before)\n            format_run(run)\n        raw_url = match.group(0)\n        url = raw_url.rstrip(\".,;)\")\n        suffix = raw_url[len(url) :]\n        add_hyperlink(paragraph, url, url)\n        if suffix:\n            run = paragraph.add_run(suffix)\n            format_run(run)\n        cursor = match.end()\n    if cursor < len(value):\n        run = paragraph.add_run(value[cursor:])\n        format_run(run)\n\n\ndef main():\n    references = collect_references()\n    document = Document()\n    section = document.sections[0]\n    section.top_margin = Cm(2.5)\n    section.bottom_margin = Cm(2.5)\n    section.left_margin = Cm(2.5)\n    section.right_margin = Cm(2.5)\n\n    title = document.add_paragraph()\n    title.alignment = WD_ALIGN_PARAGRAPH.CENTER\n    title.paragraph_format.space_after = Pt(18)\n    format_run(title.add_run(\"Referencias bibliográficas consolidadas\"), 16, True)\n\n    introduction = document.add_paragraph()\n    introduction.alignment = WD_ALIGN_PARAGRAPH.JUSTIFY\n    introduction.paragraph_format.line_spacing = 1.5\n    introduction.paragraph_format.space_after = Pt(12)\n    format_run(\n        introduction.add_run(\n            \"Referencias citadas en las versiones finales actuales de los capítulos 2, 3 y 4. \"\n            \"Se conserva la numeración utilizada en el texto y se eliminan las repeticiones entre capítulos.\"\n        )\n    )\n\n    for number in sorted(references):\n        add_reference(document, number, references[number])\n\n    document.save(OUTPUT)\n    print(OUTPUT)\n    print(f\"Referencias incluidas: {len(references)}\")\n\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    main()\n"}], "status": "completed"}}
{"record_type": "item", "metadata": {"thread_id": "019eb3a5-07e3-7163-a098-145f9d55e5f3", "turn_id": "019ef107-a69c-7682-bf58-602ad0cd4660", "item_id": "item-271", "rollout_ordinal": 2309, "created_at_ms": 1782160416532, "item_type": "contextCompaction", "updated_at_ordinal": 2309, "started_at_ms": null, "completed_at_ms": null}, "item": {"type": "contextCompaction", "id": "item-271"}}
{"record_type": "item", "metadata": {"thread_id": "019eb3a5-07e3-7163-a098-145f9d55e5f3", "turn_id": "019ef107-a69c-7682-bf58-602ad0cd4660", "item_id": "item-272", "rollout_ordinal": 2311, "created_at_ms": 1782160420719, "item_type": "agentMessage", "updated_at_ordinal": 2311, "started_at_ms": null, "completed_at_ms": null}, "item": {"type": "agentMessage", "id": "item-272", "text": "Ya consolidé las referencias presentes en las versiones finales de los capítulos 2, 3 y 4. Ahora generaré el Word y comprobaré que la numeración, los enlaces y los caracteres hayan quedado bien.", "phase": "commentary", "memoryCitation": null, "delivery": null, "questions": null}}
{"record_type": "item", "metadata": {"thread_id": "019eb3a5-07e3-7163-a098-145f9d55e5f3", "turn_id": "019ef107-a69c-7682-bf58-602ad0cd4660", "item_id": "item-273", "rollout_ordinal": 2317, "created_at_ms": 1782160428765, "item_type": "agentMessage", "updated_at_ordinal": 2317, "started_at_ms": null, "completed_at_ms": null}, "item": {"type": "agentMessage", "id": "item-273", "text": "El documento ya fue generado con 26 referencias. Haré una revisión final para confirmar que contiene desde la referencia `[5]` hasta la `[30]`, sin duplicados ni citas descartadas.", "phase": "commentary", "memoryCitation": null, "delivery": null, "questions": null}}
{"record_type": "item", "metadata": {"thread_id": "019eb3a5-07e3-7163-a098-145f9d55e5f3", "turn_id": "019ef107-a69c-7682-bf58-602ad0cd4660", "item_id": "item-274", "rollout_ordinal": 2323, "created_at_ms": 1782160440904, "item_type": "agentMessage", "updated_at_ordinal": 2323, "started_at_ms": null, "completed_at_ms": null}, "item": {"type": "agentMessage", "id": "item-274", "text": "Documento creado y revisado:\n\n[Descargar Referencias_documento_final.docx](<C:\\Users\\Diego Tapia\\Desktop\\Pene\\U\\Tesis\\tesis_karaoke\\Referencias_documento_final.docx>)\n\nIncluye las 26 referencias confirmadas `[5]–[30]` de los capítulos 2, 3 y 4. Las referencias `[1]–[4]` no aparecen en los archivos finales disponibles.", "phase": "final_answer", "memoryCitation": null, "delivery": null, "questions": null}}
{"record_type": "item", "metadata": {"thread_id": "019eb3a5-07e3-7163-a098-145f9d55e5f3", "turn_id": "019ef2c4-a9c5-7a32-84c4-57521db3912d", "item_id": "item-275", "rollout_ordinal": 2330, "created_at_ms": 1782189462124, "item_type": "contextCompaction", "updated_at_ordinal": 2330, "started_at_ms": null, "completed_at_ms": null}, "item": {"type": "contextCompaction", "id": "item-275"}}
{"record_type": "item", "metadata": {"thread_id": "019eb3a5-07e3-7163-a098-145f9d55e5f3", "turn_id": "019ef2c4-a9c5-7a32-84c4-57521db3912d", "item_id": "item-276", "rollout_ordinal": 2335, "created_at_ms": 1782189462162, "item_type": "userMessage", "updated_at_ordinal": 2335, "started_at_ms": null, "completed_at_ms": null}, "item": {"type": "userMessage", "id": "item-276", "clientId": "6848d15a-eccf-4a7f-900f-5f01af97ad68", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "prepara un documento con el indice, tambien uno con la portada basandote en alguno de los documentos de ejemplo\n", "text_elements": []}]}}
{"record_type": "item", "metadata": {"thread_id": "019eb3a5-07e3-7163-a098-145f9d55e5f3", "turn_id": "019ef2c4-a9c5-7a32-84c4-57521db3912d", "item_id": "item-277", "rollout_ordinal": 2337, "created_at_ms": 1782189469590, "item_type": "agentMessage", "updated_at_ordinal": 2337, "started_at_ms": null, "completed_at_ms": null}, "item": {"type": "agentMessage", "id": "item-277", "text": "Voy a revisar los documentos que ya quedaron en la carpeta y los ejemplos disponibles para que la portada y el índice sigan el estilo que ya vienes usando. Después genero ambos `.docx` separados y te dejo los enlaces.", "phase": "commentary", "memoryCitation": null, "delivery": null, "questions": null}}
{"record_type": "item", "metadata": {"thread_id": "019eb3a5-07e3-7163-a098-145f9d55e5f3", "turn_id": "019ef2c4-a9c5-7a32-84c4-57521db3912d", "item_id": "item-278", "rollout_ordinal": 2350, "created_at_ms": 1782189497376, "item_type": "agentMessage", "updated_at_ordinal": 2350, "started_at_ms": null, "completed_at_ms": null}, "item": {"type": "agentMessage", "id": "item-278", "text": "Ya encontré los capítulos y los documentos de ejemplo. Ahora voy a extraer títulos/estructura y revisar las portadas de referencia para armar una portada coherente, sin inventar más datos de los necesarios.", "phase": "commentary", "memoryCitation": null, "delivery": null, "questions": null}}
{"record_type": "item", "metadata": {"thread_id": "019eb3a5-07e3-7163-a098-145f9d55e5f3", "turn_id": "019ef2c4-a9c5-7a32-84c4-57521db3912d", "item_id": "item-279", "rollout_ordinal": 2360, "created_at_ms": 1782189513862, "item_type": "agentMessage", "updated_at_ordinal": 2360, "started_at_ms": null, "completed_at_ms": null}, "item": {"type": "agentMessage", "id": "item-279", "text": "Los `.docx` no tienen estilos de encabezado marcados, así que voy a construir el índice desde el contenido que ya tenemos y la estructura tentativo-final que fuimos acordando. Para la portada usaré el PDF de planificación y el formato de memoria como referencia de campos y orden.", "phase": "commentary", "memoryCitation": null, "delivery": null, "questions": null}}
{"record_type": "item", "metadata": {"thread_id": "019eb3a5-07e3-7163-a098-145f9d55e5f3", "turn_id": "019ef2c4-a9c5-7a32-84c4-57521db3912d", "item_id": "item-280", "rollout_ordinal": 2368, "created_at_ms": 1782189546735, "item_type": "agentMessage", "updated_at_ordinal": 2368, "started_at_ms": null, "completed_at_ms": null}, "item": {"type": "agentMessage", "id": "item-280", "text": "Hay un detalle menor con las rutas acentuadas al extraer texto desde PowerShell, así que voy a resolver los archivos por patrones de carpeta en vez de escribir la ruta completa. De paso reviso los primeros párrafos de los capítulos sin que se rompa la salida por símbolos musicales.", "phase": "commentary", "memoryCitation": null, "delivery": null, "questions": null}}
{"record_type": "item", "metadata": {"thread_id": "019eb3a5-07e3-7163-a098-145f9d55e5f3", "turn_id": "019ef2c4-a9c5-7a32-84c4-57521db3912d", "item_id": "item-281", "rollout_ordinal": 2376, "created_at_ms": 1782189572818, "item_type": "agentMessage", "updated_at_ordinal": 2376, "started_at_ms": null, "completed_at_ms": null}, "item": {"type": "agentMessage", "id": "item-281", "text": "Con la referencia ya clara: la portada del ejemplo usa una estructura sobria institucional, sin portada “decorativa”. Para el índice voy a generar un índice tentativo completo, compatible con lo que ya escribimos: capítulo 1, marco teórico y trabajo relacionado, metodología, desarrollo, evaluación/cierre, conclusiones, referencias y anexos.", "phase": "commentary", "memoryCitation": null, "delivery": null, "questions": null}}
{"record_type": "item", "metadata": {"thread_id": "019eb3a5-07e3-7163-a098-145f9d55e5f3", "turn_id": "019ef2c4-a9c5-7a32-84c4-57521db3912d", "item_id": "item-282", "rollout_ordinal": 2384, "created_at_ms": 1782189603568, "item_type": "agentMessage", "updated_at_ordinal": 2384, "started_at_ms": null, "completed_at_ms": null}, "item": {"type": "agentMessage", "id": "item-282", "text": "Voy a crear dos archivos nuevos: `Indice_tentativo_memoria.docx` y `Portada_memoria.docx`. Los haré editables en Word, con tipografía sobria tipo memoria y usando la portada oficial de ejemplo como guía.", "phase": "commentary", "memoryCitation": null, "delivery": null, "questions": null}}
{"record_type": "item", "metadata": {"thread_id": "019eb3a5-07e3-7163-a098-145f9d55e5f3", "turn_id": "019ef2c4-a9c5-7a32-84c4-57521db3912d", "item_id": "call_fE1UgYc7jqsAlpMDgaTBaTFM", "rollout_ordinal": 2387, "created_at_ms": 1782189677832, "item_type": "fileChange", "updated_at_ordinal": 2387, "started_at_ms": null, "completed_at_ms": null}, "item": {"type": "fileChange", "id": "call_fE1UgYc7jqsAlpMDgaTBaTFM", "changes": [{"path": "C:\\Users\\Diego Tapia\\Desktop\\Pene\\U\\Tesis\\tesis_karaoke\\docs\\generar_indice_y_portada.py", "kind": {"type": "add"}, "diff": "from pathlib import Path\n\nfrom docx import Document\nfrom docx.enum.section import WD_SECTION\nfrom docx.enum.text import WD_ALIGN_PARAGRAPH\nfrom docx.oxml import OxmlElement\nfrom docx.oxml.ns import qn\nfrom docx.shared import Cm, Pt\n\n\nROOT = Path(__file__).resolve().parents[1]\n\n\nFONT = \"Times New Roman\"\n\n\ndef set_run(run, size=12, bold=False, italic=False, all_caps=False):\n    run.font.name = FONT\n    run._element.rPr.rFonts.set(qn(\"w:eastAsia\"), FONT)\n    run.font.size = Pt(size)\n    run.bold = bold\n    run.italic = italic\n    if all_caps:\n        run.text = run.text.upper()\n\n\ndef set_paragraph(paragraph, size=12, bold=False, align=None, space_after=0):\n    if align is not None:\n        paragraph.alignment = align\n    paragraph.paragraph_format.space_after = Pt(space_after)\n    paragraph.paragraph_format.line_spacing = 1.15\n    for run in paragraph.runs:\n        set_run(run, size=size, bold=bold)\n\n\ndef set_cell_text(cell, text, size=12, bold=False, align=None):\n    cell.text = \"\"\n    p = cell.paragraphs[0]\n    p.alignment = align or WD_ALIGN_PARAGRAPH.LEFT\n    run = p.add_run(text)\n    set_run(run, size=size, bold=bold)\n    p.paragraph_format.space_after = Pt(0)\n\n\ndef clear_table_borders(table):\n    tbl = table._tbl\n    tbl_pr = tbl.tblPr\n    borders = tbl_pr.first_child_found_in(\"w:tblBorders\")\n    if borders is None:\n        borders = OxmlElement(\"w:tblBorders\")\n        tbl_pr.append(borders)\n    for edge in (\"top\", \"left\", \"bottom\", \"right\", \"insideH\", \"insideV\"):\n        tag = \"w:{}\".format(edge)\n        element = borders.find(qn(tag))\n        if element is None:\n            element = OxmlElement(tag)\n            borders.append(element)\n        element.set(qn(\"w:val\"), \"nil\")\n\n\ndef configure_document(doc):\n    section = doc.sections[0]\n    section.top_margin = Cm(2.5)\n    section.bottom_margin = Cm(2.5)\n    section.left_margin = Cm(3)\n    section.right_margin = Cm(2.5)\n    styles = doc.styles\n    normal = styles[\"Normal\"]\n    normal.font.name = FONT\n    normal._element.rPr.rFonts.set(qn(\"w:eastAsia\"), FONT)\n    normal.font.size = Pt(12)\n\n\ndef add_index_entry(doc, number, title, level=0):\n    paragraph = doc.add_paragraph()\n    paragraph.paragraph_format.left_indent = Cm(0.6 * level)\n    paragraph.paragraph_format.first_line_indent = Cm(-0.1 if level else 0)\n    paragraph.paragraph_format.space_after = Pt(1)\n    run = paragraph.add_run(f\"{number} {title}\" if number else title)\n    set_run(run, size=12, bold=(level == 0 and bool(number)))\n\n\ndef build_index():\n    doc = Document()\n    configure_document(doc)\n\n    title = doc.add_paragraph()\n    title.alignment = WD_ALIGN_PARAGRAPH.CENTER\n    run = title.add_run(\"TABLA DE CONTENIDOS\")\n    set_run(run, size=14, bold=True)\n    title.paragraph_format.space_after = Pt(18)\n\n    entries = [\n        (\"\", \"Resumen\", 0),\n        (\"\", \"Índice de figuras\", 0),\n        (\"\", \"Índice de tablas\", 0),\n        (\"1.\", \"Introducción\", 0),\n        (\"1.1.\", \"Contexto\", 1),\n        (\"1.2.\", \"Definición del problema\", 1),\n        (\"1.3.\", \"Propuesta de solución\", 1),\n        (\"1.4.\", \"Objetivos\", 1),\n        (\"1.4.1.\", \"Objetivo general\", 2),\n        (\"1.4.2.\", \"Objetivos específicos\", 2),\n        (\"1.5.\", \"Alcances y limitaciones\", 1),\n        (\"1.6.\", \"Plan de trabajo\", 1),\n        (\"1.6.1.\", \"Descripción de las etapas del proyecto\", 2),\n        (\"1.6.2.\", \"Relación entre objetivos y etapas\", 2),\n        (\"1.7.\", \"Estado actual del proyecto\", 1),\n        (\"2.\", \"Marco teórico y trabajo relacionado\", 0),\n        (\"2.1.\", \"Fundamentos musicales y vocales\", 1),\n        (\"2.1.1.\", \"Frecuencia y altura tonal\", 2),\n        (\"2.1.2.\", \"Notas musicales y octavas\", 2),\n        (\"2.1.3.\", \"Afinación y estabilidad tonal\", 2),\n        (\"2.2.\", \"Procesamiento digital de audio\", 1),\n        (\"2.2.1.\", \"Digitalización de una señal\", 2),\n        (\"2.2.2.\", \"Frecuencia de muestreo\", 2),\n        (\"2.2.3.\", \"Ventanas y bloques de audio\", 2),\n        (\"2.2.4.\", \"Ruido, silencios y filtrado\", 2),\n        (\"2.3.\", \"Estimación de frecuencia fundamental\", 1),\n        (\"2.3.1.\", \"Sonoridad y periodicidad\", 2),\n        (\"2.3.2.\", \"Estimación mediante pYIN\", 2),\n        (\"2.3.3.\", \"WORLD y Pyworld\", 2),\n        (\"2.3.4.\", \"Errores frecuentes de estimación\", 2),\n        (\"2.3.5.\", \"Criterios para el proyecto\", 2),\n        (\"2.4.\", \"Separación de fuentes musicales\", 1),\n        (\"2.4.1.\", \"Separación mediante modelos preentrenados\", 2),\n        (\"2.4.2.\", \"Spleeter\", 2),\n        (\"2.4.3.\", \"Demucs y Hybrid Transformer Demucs\", 2),\n        (\"2.4.4.\", \"Artefactos y limitaciones\", 2),\n        (\"2.4.5.\", \"Criterios para el proyecto\", 2),\n        (\"2.5.\", \"Alineación temporal mediante Dynamic Time Warping\", 1),\n        (\"2.5.1.\", \"Matriz de costos\", 2),\n        (\"2.5.2.\", \"Trayectoria de alineación\", 2),\n        (\"2.5.3.\", \"Aplicación a curvas de pitch\", 2),\n        (\"2.5.4.\", \"Limitaciones de la alineación\", 2),\n        (\"2.5.5.\", \"Criterios para el proyecto\", 2),\n        (\"2.6.\", \"Detección y caracterización de segmentos problemáticos\", 1),\n        (\"2.6.1.\", \"Evidencias locales de la interpretación\", 2),\n        (\"2.6.2.\", \"Formación dinámica de segmentos\", 2),\n        (\"2.6.3.\", \"Caracterización de problemáticas\", 2),\n        (\"2.6.4.\", \"Severidad y priorización\", 2),\n        (\"2.6.5.\", \"Criterios para el proyecto\", 2),\n        (\"2.7.\", \"Generación de retroalimentación en lenguaje natural\", 1),\n        (\"2.7.1.\", \"Representación estructurada de hallazgos\", 2),\n        (\"2.7.2.\", \"Generación mediante plantillas\", 2),\n        (\"2.7.3.\", \"Generación mediante un modelo de lenguaje\", 2),\n        (\"2.7.4.\", \"Riesgos y validación\", 2),\n        (\"2.7.5.\", \"Criterios para el proyecto\", 2),\n        (\"2.8.\", \"Seguimiento y comparación de la evolución\", 1),\n        (\"2.8.1.\", \"Persistencia de sesiones\", 2),\n        (\"2.8.2.\", \"Comparabilidad entre sesiones\", 2),\n        (\"2.8.3.\", \"Resumen de cambios\", 2),\n        (\"2.8.4.\", \"Criterios para el proyecto\", 2),\n        (\"2.9.\", \"Tecnologías consideradas\", 1),\n        (\"2.9.1.\", \"Lenguaje y procesamiento de audio\", 2),\n        (\"2.9.2.\", \"Interfaz gráfica\", 2),\n        (\"2.9.3.\", \"Almacenamiento\", 2),\n        (\"2.9.4.\", \"Distribución y dependencias\", 2),\n        (\"2.9.5.\", \"Criterios para el proyecto\", 2),\n        (\"2.10.\", \"Trabajo relacionado\", 1),\n        (\"2.10.1.\", \"Diferenciación de la propuesta\", 2),\n        (\"2.11.\", \"Síntesis del capítulo\", 1),\n        (\"3.\", \"Metodología\", 0),\n        (\"3.1.\", \"Estrategia metodológica\", 1),\n        (\"3.1.1.\", \"Adaptación de PXP al proyecto\", 2),\n        (\"3.1.2.\", \"Evidencia de aceptación por capacidad\", 2),\n        (\"3.1.3.\", \"Dependencias entre iteraciones\", 2),\n        (\"3.1.4.\", \"Tratamiento de decisiones abiertas\", 2),\n        (\"3.2.\", \"Diseño de evaluación\", 1),\n        (\"3.2.1.\", \"Conjunto de pruebas\", 2),\n        (\"3.2.2.\", \"Experimento de estimación y filtrado de pitch\", 2),\n        (\"3.2.3.\", \"Experimento de detección en tiempo real\", 2),\n        (\"3.2.4.\", \"Experimento de alineación y segmentación\", 2),\n        (\"3.2.5.\", \"Evaluación de retroalimentación e historial\", 2),\n        (\"3.2.6.\", \"Pruebas funcionales y regresión\", 2),\n        (\"3.2.7.\", \"Reproducibilidad y registro\", 2),\n        (\"3.3.\", \"Estado metodológico actual\", 1),\n        (\"3.4.\", \"Amenazas a la validez\", 1),\n        (\"3.5.\", \"Síntesis del capítulo\", 1),\n        (\"4.\", \"Desarrollo\", 0),\n        (\"4.1.\", \"Arquitectura derivada del entorno de ejecución\", 1),\n        (\"4.1.1.\", \"Despliegue físico\", 2),\n        (\"4.1.2.\", \"Arquitectura lógica actual\", 2),\n        (\"4.1.3.\", \"Flujos de ejecución\", 2),\n        (\"4.1.4.\", \"Modelo de datos\", 2),\n        (\"4.2.\", \"Implementación y decisiones actuales\", 1),\n        (\"4.2.1.\", \"Identidad y ciclo de una canción\", 2),\n        (\"4.2.2.\", \"Separación y construcción del acompañamiento\", 2),\n        (\"4.2.3.\", \"Estimación y filtrado de frecuencia fundamental\", 2),\n        (\"4.2.4.\", \"Captura, concurrencia y estado\", 2),\n        (\"4.2.5.\", \"Alineación y métricas\", 2),\n        (\"4.2.6.\", \"Visualización y persistencia\", 2),\n        (\"4.3.\", \"Evolución arquitectónica necesaria\", 1),\n        (\"4.3.1.\", \"Canal de tiempo real\", 2),\n        (\"4.3.2.\", \"Trayectoria y segmentos\", 2),\n        (\"4.3.3.\", \"Versionado para comparación histórica\", 2),\n        (\"4.3.4.\", \"Adaptadores de retroalimentación y presentación\", 2),\n        (\"4.4.\", \"Evidencia producida por el prototipo\", 1),\n        (\"4.5.\", \"Riesgos técnicos concretos\", 1),\n        (\"4.6.\", \"Síntesis del capítulo\", 1),\n        (\"5.\", \"Evaluación y resultados\", 0),\n        (\"5.1.\", \"Plan de evaluación\", 1),\n        (\"5.2.\", \"Resultados de estimación y filtrado de pitch\", 1),\n        (\"5.3.\", \"Resultados de alineación temporal\", 1),\n        (\"5.4.\", \"Resultados de detección de segmentos problemáticos\", 1),\n        (\"5.5.\", \"Resultados de retroalimentación generada\", 1),\n        (\"5.6.\", \"Resultados de comparación entre sesiones\", 1),\n        (\"5.7.\", \"Discusión de resultados\", 1),\n        (\"5.8.\", \"Síntesis del capítulo\", 1),\n        (\"6.\", \"Conclusiones\", 0),\n        (\"6.1.\", \"Conclusiones del proyecto\", 1),\n        (\"6.2.\", \"Cumplimiento de objetivos\", 1),\n        (\"6.3.\", \"Limitaciones\", 1),\n        (\"6.4.\", \"Trabajo futuro\", 1),\n        (\"\", \"Referencias\", 0),\n        (\"\", \"Anexos\", 0),\n        (\"A.\", \"Especificación de requisitos\", 1),\n        (\"B.\", \"Historias de usuario\", 1),\n        (\"C.\", \"Carta Gantt\", 1),\n        (\"D.\", \"Modelo de datos\", 1),\n        (\"E.\", \"Diagramas complementarios\", 1),\n        (\"F.\", \"Evidencia de pruebas\", 1),\n    ]\n\n    for number, title_text, level in entries:\n        add_index_entry(doc, number, title_text, level)\n\n    note = doc.add_paragraph()\n    note.paragraph_format.space_before = Pt(12)\n    note.alignment = WD_ALIGN_PARAGRAPH.JUSTIFY\n    run = note.add_run(\n        \"Nota: la numeración de páginas debe actualizarse cuando los capítulos se integren \"\n        \"en un único documento final.\"\n    )\n    set_run(run, size=10, italic=True)\n\n    path = ROOT / \"Indice_tentativo_memoria.docx\"\n    doc.save(path)\n    return path\n\n\ndef add_spacer(doc, height_pt):\n    paragraph = doc.add_paragraph()\n    paragraph.paragraph_format.space_after = Pt(height_pt)\n\n\ndef build_cover():\n    doc = Document()\n    configure_document(doc)\n    section = doc.sections[0]\n    section.top_margin = Cm(2.3)\n    section.bottom_margin = Cm(2.3)\n    section.left_margin = Cm(3)\n    section.right_margin = Cm(3)\n\n    header_lines = [\n        \"UNIVERSIDAD DE TALCA\",\n        \"FACULTAD DE INGENIERÍA\",\n        \"ESCUELA DE INGENIERÍA CIVIL EN COMPUTACIÓN\",\n    ]\n    for line in header_lines:\n        p = doc.add_paragraph()\n        p.alignment = WD_ALIGN_PARAGRAPH.CENTER\n        run = p.add_run(line)\n        set_run(run, size=12, bold=True)\n        p.paragraph_format.space_after = Pt(2)\n\n    add_spacer(doc, 72)\n\n    title = (\n        \"Sistema de análisis vocal, detección de patrones de error y \"\n        \"retroalimentación basado en procesamiento digital de señales\"\n    )\n    p = doc.add_paragraph()\n    p.alignment = WD_ALIGN_PARAGRAPH.CENTER\n    p.paragraph_format.space_after = Pt(36)\n    run = p.add_run(title)\n    set_run(run, size=18, bold=True)\n\n    p = doc.add_paragraph()\n    p.alignment = WD_ALIGN_PARAGRAPH.CENTER\n    p.paragraph_format.space_after = Pt(24)\n    run = p.add_run(\"DIEGO ALFONSO TAPIA VÁSQUEZ\")\n    set_run(run, size=13, bold=True)\n\n    table = doc.add_table(rows=3, cols=1)\n    clear_table_borders(table)\n    table.alignment = WD_ALIGN_PARAGRAPH.CENTER\n    set_cell_text(table.cell(0, 0), \"Profesor Guía: RICARDO PÉREZ\", size=12, align=WD_ALIGN_PARAGRAPH.CENTER)\n    set_cell_text(\n        table.cell(1, 0),\n        \"Memoria para optar al título de\",\n        size=12,\n        align=WD_ALIGN_PARAGRAPH.CENTER,\n    )\n    set_cell_text(\n        table.cell(2, 0),\n        \"Ingeniero Civil en Computación\",\n        size=12,\n        align=WD_ALIGN_PARAGRAPH.CENTER,\n    )\n\n    for row in table.rows:\n        row.height = Cm(0.6)\n\n    add_spacer(doc, 140)\n\n    p = doc.add_paragraph()\n    p.alignment = WD_ALIGN_PARAGRAPH.CENTER\n    run = p.add_run(\"Curicó - Chile\")\n    set_run(run, size=12)\n    p.paragraph_format.space_after = Pt(4)\n\n    p = doc.add_paragraph()\n    p.alignment = WD_ALIGN_PARAGRAPH.CENTER\n    run = p.add_run(\"junio, 2026\")\n    set_run(run, size=12)\n\n    path = ROOT / \"Portada_memoria.docx\"\n    doc.save(path)\n    return path\n\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    index_path = build_index()\n    cover_path = build_cover()\n    print(index_path)\n    print(cover_path)\n"}], "status": "completed"}}
{"record_type": "item", "metadata": {"thread_id": "019eb3a5-07e3-7163-a098-145f9d55e5f3", "turn_id": "019ef2c4-a9c5-7a32-84c4-57521db3912d", "item_id": "item-283", "rollout_ordinal": 2390, "created_at_ms": 1782189683030, "item_type": "agentMessage", "updated_at_ordinal": 2390, "started_at_ms": null, "completed_at_ms": null}, "item": {"type": "agentMessage", "id": "item-283", "text": "Ya dejé el generador listo. Ahora lo ejecuto y hago una verificación rápida de que los documentos se hayan creado con el contenido esperado.", "phase": "commentary", "memoryCitation": null, "delivery": null, "questions": null}}
{"record_type": "item", "metadata": {"thread_id": "019eb3a5-07e3-7163-a098-145f9d55e5f3", "turn_id": "019ef2c4-a9c5-7a32-84c4-57521db3912d", "item_id": "item-284", "rollout_ordinal": 2398, "created_at_ms": 1782189693066, "item_type": "agentMessage", "updated_at_ordinal": 2398, "started_at_ms": null, "completed_at_ms": null}, "item": {"type": "agentMessage", "id": "item-284", "text": "Los archivos ya fueron generados. Voy a abrirlos internamente con `python-docx` para comprobar portada, primeros apartados del índice y que no haya quedado vacío algún documento.", "phase": "commentary", "memoryCitation": null, "delivery": null, "questions": null}}
{"record_type": "item", "metadata": {"thread_id": "019eb3a5-07e3-7163-a098-145f9d55e5f3", "turn_id": "019ef2c4-a9c5-7a32-84c4-57521db3912d", "item_id": "item-285", "rollout_ordinal": 2406, "created_at_ms": 1782189701568, "item_type": "agentMessage", "updated_at_ordinal": 2406, "started_at_ms": null, "completed_at_ms": null}, "item": {"type": "agentMessage", "id": "item-285", "text": "Listo, dejé creados los dos documentos:\n\n- [Indice_tentativo_memoria.docx](<C:\\Users\\Diego Tapia\\Desktop\\Pene\\U\\Tesis\\tesis_karaoke\\Indice_tentativo_memoria.docx>)\n- [Portada_memoria.docx](<C:\\Users\\Diego Tapia\\Desktop\\Pene\\U\\Tesis\\tesis_karaoke\\Portada_memoria.docx>)\n\nEl índice quedó como estructura tentativo-final, sin paginación definitiva porque todavía no está todo unido en un solo documento. La portada la armé siguiendo el formato sobrio de memoria de la Universidad de Talca, usando los datos que aparecían en tu entrega anterior.", "phase": "final_answer", "memoryCitation": null, "delivery": null, "questions": null}}
{"record_type": "item", "metadata": {"thread_id": "019eb3a5-07e3-7163-a098-145f9d55e5f3", "turn_id": "019ef2da-cca1-72d2-8442-4cd559469056", "item_id": "item-286", "rollout_ordinal": 2413, "created_at_ms": 1782190886141, "item_type": "userMessage", "updated_at_ordinal": 2413, "started_at_ms": null, "completed_at_ms": null}, "item": {"type": "userMessage", "id": "item-286", "clientId": "37d9e11a-4810-4fe4-8e1d-342b7d678512", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "pero el capitulo 5 y 6 no están hechos, de donde salieron?\n", "text_elements": []}]}}
{"record_type": "item", "metadata": {"thread_id": "019eb3a5-07e3-7163-a098-145f9d55e5f3", "turn_id": "019ef2da-cca1-72d2-8442-4cd559469056", "item_id": "item-287", "rollout_ordinal": 2415, "created_at_ms": 1782190898620, "item_type": "agentMessage", "updated_at_ordinal": 2415, "started_at_ms": null, "completed_at_ms": null}, "item": {"type": "agentMessage", "id": "item-287", "text": "Tienes toda la razón: esos capítulos salieron de una proyección mía del documento final, no de material que ya tengamos escrito. Para que no se vea como si existieran capítulos inexistentes, voy a corregir el índice y dejarlo alineado solo con lo trabajado hasta ahora.", "phase": "commentary", "memoryCitation": null, "delivery": null, "questions": null}}
{"record_type": "item", "metadata": {"thread_id": "019eb3a5-07e3-7163-a098-145f9d55e5f3", "turn_id": "019ef2da-cca1-72d2-8442-4cd559469056", "item_id": "call_CK9ayWEsiCpXpwNSXJPX2X6J", "rollout_ordinal": 2418, "created_at_ms": 1782190905867, "item_type": "fileChange", "updated_at_ordinal": 2418, "started_at_ms": null, "completed_at_ms": null}, "item": {"type": "fileChange", "id": "call_CK9ayWEsiCpXpwNSXJPX2X6J", "changes": [{"path": "C:\\Users\\Diego Tapia\\Desktop\\Pene\\U\\Tesis\\tesis_karaoke\\docs\\generar_indice_y_portada.py", "kind": {"type": "update", "move_path": null}, "diff": "@@ -200,16 +200,2 @@\n         (\"4.6.\", \"Síntesis del capítulo\", 1),\n-        (\"5.\", \"Evaluación y resultados\", 0),\n-        (\"5.1.\", \"Plan de evaluación\", 1),\n-        (\"5.2.\", \"Resultados de estimación y filtrado de pitch\", 1),\n-        (\"5.3.\", \"Resultados de alineación temporal\", 1),\n-        (\"5.4.\", \"Resultados de detección de segmentos problemáticos\", 1),\n-        (\"5.5.\", \"Resultados de retroalimentación generada\", 1),\n-        (\"5.6.\", \"Resultados de comparación entre sesiones\", 1),\n-        (\"5.7.\", \"Discusión de resultados\", 1),\n-        (\"5.8.\", \"Síntesis del capítulo\", 1),\n-        (\"6.\", \"Conclusiones\", 0),\n-        (\"6.1.\", \"Conclusiones del proyecto\", 1),\n-        (\"6.2.\", \"Cumplimiento de objetivos\", 1),\n-        (\"6.3.\", \"Limitaciones\", 1),\n-        (\"6.4.\", \"Trabajo futuro\", 1),\n         (\"\", \"Referencias\", 0),\n@@ -231,4 +217,4 @@\n     run = note.add_run(\n-        \"Nota: la numeración de páginas debe actualizarse cuando los capítulos se integren \"\n-        \"en un único documento final.\"\n+        \"Nota: este índice corresponde al estado actual del documento. La numeración de páginas \"\n+        \"debe actualizarse cuando los capítulos se integren en un único archivo.\"\n     )\n"}], "status": "completed"}}
{"record_type": "item", "metadata": {"thread_id": "019eb3a5-07e3-7163-a098-145f9d55e5f3", "turn_id": "019ef2da-cca1-72d2-8442-4cd559469056", "item_id": "item-288", "rollout_ordinal": 2421, "created_at_ms": 1782190913839, "item_type": "agentMessage", "updated_at_ordinal": 2421, "started_at_ms": null, "completed_at_ms": null}, "item": {"type": "agentMessage", "id": "item-288", "text": "Voy a regenerar el índice con esa corrección. Dejo fuera los capítulos 5 y 6 para que el documento represente solo lo efectivamente avanzado.", "phase": "commentary", "memoryCitation": null, "delivery": null, "questions": null}}
{"record_type": "item", "metadata": {"thread_id": "019eb3a5-07e3-7163-a098-145f9d55e5f3", "turn_id": "019ef2da-cca1-72d2-8442-4cd559469056", "item_id": "item-289", "rollout_ordinal": 2429, "created_at_ms": 1782190923566, "item_type": "agentMessage", "updated_at_ordinal": 2429, "started_at_ms": null, "completed_at_ms": null}, "item": {"type": "agentMessage", "id": "item-289", "text": "Word parece tener abierto el índice anterior, así que no pude sobrescribirlo. Para evitar pelear con el archivo bloqueado, voy a generar una versión corregida con otro nombre y mantener el anterior intacto.", "phase": "commentary", "memoryCitation": null, "delivery": null, "questions": null}}
{"record_type": "item", "metadata": {"thread_id": "019eb3a5-07e3-7163-a098-145f9d55e5f3", "turn_id": "019ef2da-cca1-72d2-8442-4cd559469056", "item_id": "call_KLDK9sOhrulI6i9FOM8iFOLb", "rollout_ordinal": 2432, "created_at_ms": 1782190924803, "item_type": "fileChange", "updated_at_ordinal": 2432, "started_at_ms": null, "completed_at_ms": null}, "item": {"type": "fileChange", "id": "call_KLDK9sOhrulI6i9FOM8iFOLb", "changes": [{"path": "C:\\Users\\Diego Tapia\\Desktop\\Pene\\U\\Tesis\\tesis_karaoke\\docs\\generar_indice_y_portada.py", "kind": {"type": "update", "move_path": null}, "diff": "@@ -222,3 +222,3 @@\n \n-    path = ROOT / \"Indice_tentativo_memoria.docx\"\n+    path = ROOT / \"Indice_estado_actual_memoria.docx\"\n     doc.save(path)\n"}], "status": "completed"}}
{"record_type": "item", "metadata": {"thread_id": "019eb3a5-07e3-7163-a098-145f9d55e5f3", "turn_id": "019ef2da-cca1-72d2-8442-4cd559469056", "item_id": "item-290", "rollout_ordinal": 2435, "created_at_ms": 1782190930243, "item_type": "agentMessage", "updated_at_ordinal": 2435, "started_at_ms": null, "completed_at_ms": null}, "item": {"type": "agentMessage", "id": "item-290", "text": "Ahora genero solo el índice corregido y verifico que ya no aparezcan los capítulos 5 ni 6.", "phase": "commentary", "memoryCitation": null, "delivery": null, "questions": null}}
{"record_type": "item", "metadata": {"thread_id": "019eb3a5-07e3-7163-a098-145f9d55e5f3", "turn_id": "019ef2da-cca1-72d2-8442-4cd559469056", "item_id": "item-291", "rollout_ordinal": 2443, "created_at_ms": 1782190940295, "item_type": "agentMessage", "updated_at_ordinal": 2443, "started_at_ms": null, "completed_at_ms": null}, "item": {"type": "agentMessage", "id": "item-291", "text": "La generación ya terminó; como la verificación corrió en paralelo, alcanzó a listar antes de que apareciera el archivo nuevo. Hago una comprobación final secuencial para revisar el contenido.", "phase": "commentary", "memoryCitation": null, "delivery": null, "questions": null}}
{"record_type": "item", "metadata": {"thread_id": "019eb3a5-07e3-7163-a098-145f9d55e5f3", "turn_id": "019ef2da-cca1-72d2-8442-4cd559469056", "item_id": "item-292", "rollout_ordinal": 2450, "created_at_ms": 1782190944868, "item_type": "agentMessage", "updated_at_ordinal": 2450, "started_at_ms": null, "completed_at_ms": null}, "item": {"type": "agentMessage", "id": "item-292", "text": "Sí, tienes razón. Los capítulos 5 y 6 salieron de una proyección mía del documento final: normalmente después de desarrollo vendrían evaluación/resultados y conclusiones, pero todavía no los hemos trabajado, así que no correspondía dejarlos como parte del índice actual.\n\nYa corregí eso y generé una versión nueva sin esos capítulos:\n\n[Indice_estado_actual_memoria.docx](<C:\\Users\\Diego Tapia\\Desktop\\Pene\\U\\Tesis\\tesis_karaoke\\Indice_estado_actual_memoria.docx>)\n\nEl índice ahora llega hasta el capítulo 4, luego referencias y anexos. El archivo anterior quedó intacto porque probablemente estaba abierto en Word y no se podía sobrescribir.", "phase": "final_answer", "memoryCitation": null, "delivery": null, "questions": null}}
{"record_type": "item", "metadata": {"thread_id": "019eb3a5-07e3-7163-a098-145f9d55e5f3", "turn_id": "019ef2e3-f7f1-7ec1-bf8d-b7f3cd9fe1da", "item_id": "item-293", "rollout_ordinal": 2457, "created_at_ms": 1782191487290, "item_type": "userMessage", "updated_at_ordinal": 2457, "started_at_ms": null, "completed_at_ms": null}, "item": {"type": "userMessage", "id": "item-293", "clientId": "3964e498-2bc0-49ca-9414-513ece02a9fa", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "\n# Files mentioned by the user:\n\n## Carta Gantt.xlsx: C:/Users/Diego Tapia/Desktop/Pene/U/13avo semestre/Formulación/Informe final/Documento/Carta Gantt.xlsx\n\n## Documento final.docx: C:/Users/Diego Tapia/Desktop/Pene/U/13avo semestre/Formulación/Informe final/Documento/Documento final.docx\n\n## Especificacion de Requisitos.docx: C:/Users/Diego Tapia/Desktop/Pene/U/13avo semestre/Formulación/Informe final/Documento/Especificacion de Requisitos.docx\n\n## Historias de Usuario.docx: C:/Users/Diego Tapia/Desktop/Pene/U/13avo semestre/Formulación/Informe final/Documento/Historias de Usuario.docx\n\n## Modelo de datos.png: C:/Users/Diego Tapia/Desktop/Pene/U/13avo semestre/Formulación/Informe final/Documento/Modelo de datos.png\n\n## My request for Codex:\nactualmente de esto se compondría mi entrega, analiza que puede faltar, que inconcistencias hay, etc\n", "text_elements": []}, {"type": "localImage", "detail": null, "path": "C:\\Users\\Diego Tapia\\Desktop\\Pene\\U\\13avo semestre\\Formulación\\Informe final\\Documento\\Modelo de datos.png"}]}}
{"record_type": "item", "metadata": {"thread_id": "019eb3a5-07e3-7163-a098-145f9d55e5f3", "turn_id": "019ef2e3-f7f1-7ec1-bf8d-b7f3cd9fe1da", "item_id": "item-294", "rollout_ordinal": 2459, "created_at_ms": 1782191505206, "item_type": "agentMessage", "updated_at_ordinal": 2459, "started_at_ms": null, "completed_at_ms": null}, "item": {"type": "agentMessage", "id": "item-294", "text": "Voy a revisar los cuatro documentos y la carta Gantt como un paquete de entrega, no como archivos aislados. Me fijaré en estructura, coherencia entre requisitos/historias/modelo de datos, referencias, figuras/tablas y cosas que podrían llamar la atención del profesor.", "phase": "commentary", "memoryCitation": null, "delivery": null, "questions": null}}
{"record_type": "item", "metadata": {"thread_id": "019eb3a5-07e3-7163-a098-145f9d55e5f3", "turn_id": "019ef2e3-f7f1-7ec1-bf8d-b7f3cd9fe1da", "item_id": "item-295", "rollout_ordinal": 2469, "created_at_ms": 1782191546680, "item_type": "agentMessage", "updated_at_ordinal": 2469, "started_at_ms": null, "completed_at_ms": null}, "item": {"type": "agentMessage", "id": "item-295", "text": "Ya vi una alerta visual importante en el modelo de datos: aparecen tablas `users`, `posts` y `follows`, que parecen venir de una plantilla de dbdiagram y no pertenecen al proyecto. Ahora revisaré el documento final y los anexos para ver si hay otros choques de ese tipo.", "phase": "commentary", "memoryCitation": null, "delivery": null, "questions": null}}
{"record_type": "item", "metadata": {"thread_id": "019eb3a5-07e3-7163-a098-145f9d55e5f3", "turn_id": "019ef2e3-f7f1-7ec1-bf8d-b7f3cd9fe1da", "item_id": "item-296", "rollout_ordinal": 2479, "created_at_ms": 1782191583443, "item_type": "agentMessage", "updated_at_ordinal": 2479, "started_at_ms": null, "completed_at_ms": null}, "item": {"type": "agentMessage", "id": "item-296", "text": "La extracción falló por la ruta con tilde en `Formulación`, clásico detalle de Windows al pasar texto por stdin. Lo esquivo buscando la carpeta con patrón `Formulaci*`, así podemos leer los documentos sin tocar nada.", "phase": "commentary", "memoryCitation": null, "delivery": null, "questions": null}}
{"record_type": "item", "metadata": {"thread_id": "019eb3a5-07e3-7163-a098-145f9d55e5f3", "turn_id": "019ef2e3-f7f1-7ec1-bf8d-b7f3cd9fe1da", "item_id": "item-297", "rollout_ordinal": 2489, "created_at_ms": 1782191632801, "item_type": "agentMessage", "updated_at_ordinal": 2489, "started_at_ms": null, "completed_at_ms": null}, "item": {"type": "agentMessage", "id": "item-297", "text": "Hasta aquí hay varias señales útiles: el documento final sí tiene referencias completas [1]–[30] e imágenes/captions consistentes, pero también hay restos de texto de trabajo y el capítulo 1 parte directo en 1.1. Voy a ubicar esos fragmentos exactos y revisar la trazabilidad de requisitos/historias.", "phase": "commentary", "memoryCitation": null, "delivery": null, "questions": null}}
{"record_type": "item", "metadata": {"thread_id": "019eb3a5-07e3-7163-a098-145f9d55e5f3", "turn_id": "019ef2e3-f7f1-7ec1-bf8d-b7f3cd9fe1da", "item_id": "item-298", "rollout_ordinal": 2499, "created_at_ms": 1782191661577, "item_type": "agentMessage", "updated_at_ordinal": 2499, "started_at_ms": null, "completed_at_ms": null}, "item": {"type": "agentMessage", "id": "item-298", "text": "La carta Gantt se ve bien en el resumen general: declara corte en semana 15, 16/45 requisitos completos y 35,6% de avance. Estoy afinando ahora qué cosas son realmente problema y cuáles son aceptables como “decisiones pendientes” dentro de una entrega de 30%.", "phase": "commentary", "memoryCitation": null, "delivery": null, "questions": null}}
{"record_type": "item", "metadata": {"thread_id": "019eb3a5-07e3-7163-a098-145f9d55e5f3", "turn_id": "019ef2e3-f7f1-7ec1-bf8d-b7f3cd9fe1da", "item_id": "item-299", "rollout_ordinal": 2509, "created_at_ms": 1782191669681, "item_type": "agentMessage", "updated_at_ordinal": 2509, "started_at_ms": null, "completed_at_ms": null}, "item": {"type": "agentMessage", "id": "item-299", "text": "Ya tengo el cuadro general. Haré el cierre como revisión crítica: primero lo que conviene corregir sí o sí, luego ajustes recomendables y finalmente lo que se ve sólido para la entrega.", "phase": "commentary", "memoryCitation": null, "delivery": null, "questions": null}}
{"record_type": "item", "metadata": {"thread_id": "019eb3a5-07e3-7163-a098-145f9d55e5f3", "turn_id": "019ef2e3-f7f1-7ec1-bf8d-b7f3cd9fe1da", "item_id": "item-300", "rollout_ordinal": 2518, "created_at_ms": 1782191703357, "item_type": "agentMessage", "updated_at_ordinal": 2518, "started_at_ms": null, "completed_at_ms": null}, "item": {"type": "agentMessage", "id": "item-300", "text": "Pequeña corrección a mi lectura anterior: el documento final sí contiene portada e índice al inicio. Lo que veo ahora es que el índice está escrito manualmente, no con estilos de Word, y aparece “Resumen” como ítem aunque no encuentro todavía una sección de resumen desarrollada.", "phase": "commentary", "memoryCitation": null, "delivery": null, "questions": null}}
{"record_type": "item", "metadata": {"thread_id": "019eb3a5-07e3-7163-a098-145f9d55e5f3", "turn_id": "019ef2e3-f7f1-7ec1-bf8d-b7f3cd9fe1da", "item_id": "item-301", "rollout_ordinal": 2532, "created_at_ms": 1782191785635, "item_type": "agentMessage", "updated_at_ordinal": 2532, "started_at_ms": null, "completed_at_ms": null}, "item": {"type": "agentMessage", "id": "item-301", "text": "Sí, con esos archivos la entrega está bastante armada, pero hay algunas cosas que corregiría antes de entregar.\n\n**Correcciones importantes**\n\n1. En [Modelo de datos.png](<C:\\Users\\Diego Tapia\\Desktop\\Pene\\U\\13avo semestre\\Formulación\\Informe final\\Documento\\Modelo de datos.png>) aparecen tablas `users`, `posts` y `follows`. Eso parece venir de la plantilla de dbdiagram.io y no corresponde a tu sistema. Hay que eliminarlas sí o sí.\n\n2. En [Documento final.docx](<C:\\Users\\Diego Tapia\\Desktop\\Pene\\U\\13avo semestre\\Formulación\\Informe final\\Documento\\Documento final.docx>) quedó un texto de trabajo:  \n   “La figura puede presentar el siguiente contenido:”  \n   Está después de la Figura 1.2. Hay que borrarlo porque se nota como instrucción interna.\n\n3. El índice incluye `Resumen`, `Índice de figuras` e `Índice de tablas`, pero no vi esas secciones desarrolladas como tal. Tienes dos opciones: agregarlas formalmente o sacarlas del índice para esta entrega.\n\n4. El índice está escrito manualmente y sin números de página. No es fatal para una entrega de avance, pero en el ejemplo de memoria sí aparece con paginación. Si quieres que se vea más serio, conviene generar índice automático en Word o al menos agregar números de página manuales.\n\n5. En la carpeta hay archivos temporales de Word tipo `~$cumento final.docx`, `~$quisitos.docx`, etc. No los incluyas en la entrega ni en un `.zip`.\n\n**Inconsistencias menores**\n\n- La carta Gantt dice que “Definir modelo de datos y tecnología de persistencia” está pendiente, pero ya estás entregando un modelo de datos. Yo lo dejaría como “Parcial” o cambiaría el nombre a “Implementar y validar modelo de datos”.\n\n- En la Gantt aparece “Diseñar mockups”, pero en el documento dices que todavía no se diseñarán pantallas ni mockups. No es grave porque está planificado para después, pero si quieres ser coherente con lo conversado, cambiaría esa tarea a “Definir tecnología y lineamientos de interfaz”.\n\n- `RNF15 Distribución` aparece como completado en la auditoría de requisitos, aunque el ejecutable queda pendiente. Puede defenderse porque hoy se ejecuta localmente con Python/BAT, pero para evitar discusión yo lo marcaría como “Parcial”.\n\n- El modelo de datos es bueno conceptualmente, pero se ve muy pequeño y ancho para Word. Recomiendo exportarlo sin espacios vacíos, sin la marca visual de dbdiagram si es posible, y quizá dividirlo en dos figuras: datos principales y análisis/retroalimentación.\n\n**Lo que está bien**\n\n- El documento final sí tiene capítulos 1 a 4, referencias [1]–[30], 15 imágenes y 13 tablas/cuadros.\n- Los requisitos están completos y ordenados: 29 funcionales + 16 no funcionales = 45.\n- La carta Gantt calza con el avance: semana 15, 35,6% de requisitos completados y más del 30% exigido.\n- Las historias de usuario cubren bien el flujo principal: catálogo, preparación, canto, tiempo real, comparación, segmentos, feedback e historial.\n- Está bien que LLM, ejecutable, SQLite/interfaz final queden como decisiones pendientes; eso está explicado de forma razonable.\n\nMi recomendación: antes de entregar, arreglaría primero el modelo de datos, borraría el texto residual de la Figura 1.2, limpiaría los temporales y decidiría si agregas o eliminas `Resumen`, `Índice de figuras` e `Índice de tablas`. Con eso la entrega queda mucho más defendible.", "phase": "final_answer", "memoryCitation": null, "delivery": null, "questions": null}}
{"record_type": "item", "metadata": {"thread_id": "019eb3a5-07e3-7163-a098-145f9d55e5f3", "turn_id": "019ef2e8-881e-7010-9204-43df8c5f1c0c", "item_id": "item-302", "rollout_ordinal": 2539, "created_at_ms": 1782191786084, "item_type": "userMessage", "updated_at_ordinal": 2539, "started_at_ms": null, "completed_at_ms": null}, "item": {"type": "userMessage", "id": "item-302", "clientId": "a5a69f92-75fc-48bf-a546-f7a16baf20a7", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "para\n", "text_elements": []}]}}
{"record_type": "item", "metadata": {"thread_id": "019eb3a5-07e3-7163-a098-145f9d55e5f3", "turn_id": "019ef2e8-881e-7010-9204-43df8c5f1c0c", "item_id": "item-303", "rollout_ordinal": 2540, "created_at_ms": 1782191790208, "item_type": "agentMessage", "updated_at_ordinal": 2540, "started_at_ms": null, "completed_at_ms": null}, "item": {"type": "agentMessage", "id": "item-303", "text": "Paro. No hago más cambios ni análisis por ahora.", "phase": "final_answer", "memoryCitation": null, "delivery": null, "questions": null}}
